{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VKbcp78P53YM1shk5Xkd7o","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"L0 Exclusion Removal Ablation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"移除 L0 排除约束，仅保留 max_2bit=8，验证 solver 纯粹从 profiling data 自动发现 L0 敏感结构。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"solver_auto_assigns_8bit_to_L0\": true,\n7\t      \"ppl_without_l0_exclusion\": 10.91,\n8\t      \"ppl_with_l0_exclusion\": 10.91,\n9\t      \"delta\": 0.0,\n10\t      \"l0_heads_assigned_8bit\": 4,\n11\t      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n12\t    },\n13\t    \"tables\": [\n14\t      {\n15\t        \"caption\": \"Table: L0 Exclusion Ablation (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n16\t        \"rows\": [\n17\t          {\n18\t            \"condition\": \"MCKP + L0 exclusion + max_2bit=8\",\n19\t            \"ppl\": 10.91,\n20\t            \"l0_bit\": \"8-bit (hard-coded)\",\n21\t            \"note\": \"原始设置\"\n22\t          },\n23\t          {\n24\t            \"condition\": \"MCKP + max_2bit=8 only\",\n25\t            \"ppl\": 10.91,\n26\t            \"l0_bit\": \"8-bit (solver-discovered)\",\n27\t            \"note\": \"solver 自动分配\"\n28\t          }\n29\t        ]\n30\t      }\n31\t    ],\n32\t    \"figures\": [],\n33\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 评价：supportive but minor。在 median 档中被视为 completeness ablation  而非核心证据。reviewer 可能建议移到 appendix。不影响主要 claim 但增加 paper 完整性。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下该结果被 reviewer 认可为 neat ablation——solver 自动发现 L0 是最敏感的层， 不需要手动排除。但 reviewer 会指出这只在 Qwen 上验证（L0 dominance ratio=26×）， 对于 L0 dominance 低的架构（Yi 0.07，Mistral 1.74）solver 是否同样能自动发现正确结构 缺少验证。一位 reviewer 可能注释 \\\"this is expected — L0 has the largest profiling delta  by far, so any reasonable solver would protect it.\\\" 不会成为主要 objection，但也不会 被视为独立贡献。\\n\"\n34\t  },\n35\t  {\n36\t    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B Full Pipeline Replication\",\n37\t    \"description\": \"在 Llama-3.1-8B（GQA 4:1）上复制完整 pipeline——profiling、constrained MCKP、PPL 评估。 测试跨架构泛化性。\\n\",\n38\t    \"results\": {\n39\t      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 8.09,\n40\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 8.47,\n41\t      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 8.45,\n42\t      \"delta_vs_uniform_pct\": 0.2,\n43\t      \"delta_vs_uniform_ppl\": 0.02,\n44\t      \"memory_ratio\": 0.25,\n45\t      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:2, 4:253, 8:1}\",\n46\t      \"natural_2bit_count\": 2,\n47\t      \"constraint_binds\": false,\n48\t      \"unconstrained_degradation_ratio\": 1.07,\n49\t      \"top5_concentration\": 0.57,\n50\t      \"distribution_shape\": \"Spike\"\n51\t    },\n52\t    \"tables\": [\n53\t      {\n54\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Llama-3.1-8B Pipeline Results (budget=0.25)\",\n55\t        \"rows\": [\n56\t          {\n57\t            \"method\": \"BF16 baseline\",\n58\t            \"ppl\": 8.09,\n59\t            \"bits\": \"16\",\n60\t            \"note\": \"\"\n61\t          },\n62\t          {\n63\t            \"method\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n64\t            \"ppl\": 8.47,\n65\t            \"bits\": \"4.0\",\n66\t            \"note\": \"\"\n67\t          },\n68\t          {\n69\t            \"method\": \"Unconstrained MCKP\",\n70\t            \"ppl\": 8.63,\n71\t            \"bits\": \"mixed\",\n72\t            \"note\": \"1.07× baseline\"\n73\t          },\n74\t          {\n75\t            \"method\": \"Constrained MCKP (k=8)\",\n76\t            \"ppl\": 8.45,\n77\t            \"bits\": \"{2:2, 4:253, 8:1}\",\n78\t            \"note\": \"+0.2% vs uniform\"\n79\t          }\n80\t        ]\n81\t      }\n82\t    ],\n83\t    \"figures\": [],\n84\t    \"analysis\": \"Median reviewer 会同时肯定和批评：肯定 honest reporting of negative result， 批评 \\\"if 7/8 architectures show no benefit, this is not a method paper — it's an  analysis paper that happens to find one architecture where optimization helps.\\\"  这强化了 reframe 为 empirical analysis 的需要。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，Llama 的 marginal 结果（+0.2% vs uniform）成为 reviewer 攻击点之一。 reviewer 会写 \\\"the method provides essentially no benefit on Llama — the +0.2%  improvement is within noise.\\\" Llama 的 spike distribution（L2H5 单个 outlier 主导， t₁/t₅≈0.85）导致 solver 只选择 2 个 head 做 2-bit，constraint 从不触发（natural k=2 < max_2bit=8）， MCKP 优化空间极小。这解释了为什么 PPL 差异几乎为零。但从 compounding 角度， unconstrained 仍然 1.07× baseline，说明即使 mild 情况下 solver 仍会略微 over-allocate。 Reviewer 会要求诚实报告 \\\"no benefit\\\" 而非 spin 为 positive。在 median 档中， 这个 negative result 本身不被反对——reviewer 反对的是用 8 个架构中只有 1 个 positive  来声称 method 有效。\\n\"\n85\t  },\n86\t  {\n87\t    \"name\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 Full Pipeline Replication\",\n88\t    \"description\": \"在 Mistral-7B-v0.3 上复制完整 pipeline。不同架构家族，建立跨架构有效性。\\n\",\n89\t    \"results\": {\n90\t      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 7.035,\n91\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 7.131,\n92\t      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 7.165,\n93\t      \"delta_vs_uniform_pct\": -0.5,\n94\t      \"delta_vs_uniform_ppl\": -0.034,\n95\t      \"memory_ratio\": 0.25,\n96\t      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:4, 4:252}\",\n97\t      \"unconstrained_degradation_ratio\": 1.08,\n98\t      \"top5_concentration\": 0.22,\n99\t      \"distribution_shape\": \"Flat\",\n100\t      \"k_ablation_monotonic\": true,\n101\t      \"best_k_still_worse_than_uniform\": true\n102\t    },\n103\t    \"tables\": [\n104\t      {\n105\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Mistral-7B-v0.3 k-Ablation (budget=0.25)\",\n106\t        \"rows\": [\n107\t          {\n108\t            \"k\": 4,\n109\t            \"ppl\": 7.165,\n110\t            \"n_2bit\": 4,\n111\t            \"note\": \"best constrained, still > uniform\"\n112\t          },\n113\t          {\n114\t            \"k\": 8,\n115\t            \"ppl\": 7.2,\n116\t            \"n_2bit\": 8,\n117\t            \"note\": \"\"\n118\t          },\n119\t          {\n120\t            \"k\": 16,\n121\t            \"ppl\": 7.311,\n122\t            \"n_2bit\": 16,\n123\t            \"note\": \"\"\n124\t          },\n125\t          {\n126\t            \"k\": \"uniform\",\n127\t            \"ppl\": 7.131,\n128\t            \"n_2bit\": 0,\n129\t            \"note\": \"optimal for Mistral\"\n130\t          }\n131\t        ]\n132\t      }\n133\t    ],\n134\t    \"figures\": [],\n135\t    \"analysis\": \"在 median 档中，Mistral negative result 既是弱点也是优势。弱点：method 不 work。 优势：honest negative result 增加 credibility，且支持 diagnostic 的必要性—— 如果没有 diagnostic，practitioners 会浪费 profiling 时间在 Mistral 这样的模型上。 Reviewer 2 (偏方法) 会将此作为 \\\"method only works on Qwen\\\" 的证据。 Reviewer 3 (偏分析) 会认可这增加了 paper 的科学价值。\\n\\n\\nMistral 是最强 negative case：MCKP 在所有 k 值下都 worse than uniform。 PPL 随 k 单调递增（k=4: 7.165, k=8: 7.200, k=18: 7.323），profiler 报告近零  sensitivity 差异（concentration=0.22, CV=1.31）。这表明 Mistral 的 KV head  sensitivity 高度均匀——没有 head 从 2-bit downgrade 中获益。Median reviewer  会将此视为 \\\"method failure on flat architectures\\\" 和 \\\"proof that uniform 4-bit  is optimal when profiler gives zero signal.\\\" 对 compounding claim 仍有帮助： unconstrained 1.08× 表明即使 flat distribution，solver 仍 over-allocate  2-bit heads（42/256=16.4%）。但 reviewer 会质疑 \\\"1.08× is hardly catastrophic  — this is within the range where a practitioner wouldn't even notice.\\\"\\n\"\n136\t  },\n137\t  {\n138\t    \"name\": \"Compounding Effect Characterization Sweep\",\n139\t    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上扫 max_2bit 从 0 到 112，绘制 PPL vs max_2bit 曲线， 确定 compounding 阈值。建立 cardinality constraint 的 principled 基础。\\n\",\n140\t    \"results\": {\n141\t      \"k0_ppl\": 9.81,\n142\t      \"k8_ppl\": 10.05,\n143\t      \"k16_ppl\": 10.42,\n144\t      \"k32_ppl\": 11.6,\n145\t      \"k64_ppl\": 23.22,\n146\t      \"k112_ppl\": 98.75,\n147\t      \"compounding_threshold_k\": 16,\n148\t      \"max_compounding_ratio\": 10.07,\n149\t      \"curve_shape\": \"superlinear after k≈16, exponential after k≈48\",\n150\t      \"safe_k_range\": \"k≤8 universally <2.5% degradation\"\n151\t    },\n152\t    \"tables\": [\n153\t      {\n154\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Compounding Sweep (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n155\t        \"rows\": [\n156\t          {\n157\t            \"k\": 0,\n158\t            \"ppl\": 9.81,\n159\t            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"1.00×\"\n160\t          },\n161\t          {\n162\t            \"k\": 8,\n163\t            \"ppl\": 10.05,\n164\t            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"1.02×\"\n165\t          },\n166\t          {\n167\t            \"k\": 16,\n168\t            \"ppl\": 10.42,\n169\t            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"1.06×\"\n170\t          },\n171\t          {\n172\t            \"k\": 32,\n173\t            \"ppl\": 11.6,\n174\t            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"1.18×\"\n175\t          },\n176\t          {\n177\t            \"k\": 64,\n178\t            \"ppl\": 23.22,\n179\t            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"2.37×\"\n180\t          },\n181\t          {\n182\t            \"k\": 112,\n183\t            \"ppl\": 98.75,\n184\t            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"10.07×\"\n185\t          }\n186\t        ]\n187\t      }\n188\t    ],\n189\t    \"figures\": [],\n190\t    \"analysis\": \"Median reviewer 的核心反馈：compounding effect 是 real and well-characterized， 但 novelty 因 RateQuant Appendix M 打折。建议在 related work 中显式讨论  \\\"RateQuant acknowledges compounding in Appendix M but does not characterize the  threshold or provide a fix — our sweep provides the first quantitative mapping.\\\"  三架构对比增加说服力：Qwen 的 U-shape（optimal k=8）、Llama 的 flat profile （natural k=2, constraint irrelevant）、Mistral 的 monotonic increase（every  2-bit head hurts）展示了 architecture-dependent compounding behavior。\\n\\n\\nCompounding sweep 是 median 档中最被认可的实验——提供了 compounding 效应的 定量证据。PPL 在 k≤8 时近线性增长（9.81→10.05, +2.4%），k=16-32 开始加速 （10.42→11.60），k≥48 后指数爆炸（23.22→98.75）。这条曲线是 \\\"principled  basis for constraint selection\\\" 的核心证据。但 median reviewer 会有两个质疑： (1) \\\"这条曲线只在 Qwen 上做了——其他架构的阈值可能完全不同\\\"（A2）， (2) \\\"RateQuant Appendix M 已经 acknowledge compounding，这个 sweep 只是 quantified 了已知现象\\\"（A1）。需要补充 Llama 和 Mistral 的 compounding sweep  来部分 address (1)——实际已有数据（llama_compounding_sweep, mistral_compounding_sweep_v2） 可以回应。Reviewer 对 k≤8 safety 的 claim 会接受，但会要求去掉 \\\"universally safe\\\"  改为 \\\"safe across all tested architectures.\\\"\\n\"\n191\t  },\n192\t  {\n193\t    \"name\": \"Budget Sweep (2×/4×/8× Compression)\",\n194\t    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上测试 2×/4×/8× 压缩比下的 constrained MCKP vs uniform baseline。\\n\",\n195\t    \"results\": {\n196\t      \"budget_0.5_mckp_ppl\": 9.85,\n197\t      \"budget_0.5_uniform_ppl\": 9.86,\n198\t      \"budget_0.5_delta_pct\": 0.1,\n199\t      \"budget_0.25_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n200\t      \"budget_0.25_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n201\t      \"budget_0.25_delta_pct\": 29.4,\n202\t      \"budget_0.125_mckp_ppl\": 57.6,\n203\t      \"budget_0.125_uniform_2bit_ppl\": 2643.77,\n204\t      \"budget_0.125_delta_ratio\": \"45.9×\",\n205\t      \"compression_amplifies_benefit\": true\n206\t    },\n207\t    \"tables\": [\n208\t      {\n209\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Budget Sweep (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n210\t        \"rows\": [\n211\t          {\n212\t            \"compression\": \"2× (budget=0.5)\",\n213\t            \"mckp_ppl\": 9.85,\n214\t            \"uniform_ppl\": 9.86,\n215\t            \"delta\": \"~0%\"\n216\t          },\n217\t          {\n218\t            \"compression\": \"4× (budget=0.25)\",\n219\t            \"mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n220\t            \"uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n221\t            \"delta\": \"29.4%\"\n222\t          },\n223\t          {\n224\t            \"compression\": \"8× (budget=0.125)\",\n225\t            \"mckp_ppl\": 57.6,\n226\t            \"uniform_ppl\": 2643.77,\n227\t            \"delta\": \"45.9×\"\n228\t          }\n229\t        ]\n230\t      }\n231\t    ],\n232\t    \"figures\": [],\n233\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中被部分接受。Reviewer 认可 practical implication（高压缩比下 constraint  essential），但质疑 moderate compression（主要应用场景）下只有 Qwen 获益的泛化性。 建议补充 Llama/Mistral 的 budget sweep 至少在 8× 压缩点。\\n\\n\\nBudget sweep 展示了核心趋势：压缩越激进，constrained MCKP vs uniform 的差距越大。 在 2× 压缩下差异几乎为零（都接近 baseline），4× 时 MCKP 优势 29.4%，8× 时 MCKP 57.60 vs uniform 2643.77（45×差距）。Median reviewer 会认可 aggressive  compression 的 practical value（\\\"at 8× compression, the constraint is the difference  between usable and unusable\\\"），但会指出：(a) 2× 结果说明 moderate compression 下 benefit 主要来自 Qwen 的 spread pattern 而非 method 本身，(b) 8× 的 PPL=57.60  虽远好于 2643.77，但 absolute 值仍然很高——\\\"is a 57.60 PPL model actually usable?\\\"  需要补充 aggressive compression 下的 downstream task 评估。(c) 只在 Qwen 上做了 full sweep，Llama 的 aggressive compression 数据（57.60 vs 2643.77）虽有但 仅一个点，不是 sweep。\\n\"\n234\t  },\n235\t  {\n236\t    \"name\": \"High-Resolution Profiling\",\n237\t    \"description\": \"64 seq × 2048 tokens 的高分辨率 profiling（vs 16×512），验证更好的 profiling  是否改善 solver allocation。\\n\",\n238\t    \"results\": {\n239\t      \"hires_constrained_ppl_bf16\": 10.91,\n240\t      \"lowres_constrained_ppl_bf16\": 11.23,\n241\t      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 9.81,\n242\t      \"improvement_vs_lowres\": 0.32,\n243\t      \"improvement_pct\": 2.8,\n244\t      \"hires_nonzero_2bit_heads\": 100,\n245\t      \"lowres_nonzero_2bit_heads\": 37,\n246\t      \"allocation_diff_count\": 8,\n247\t      \"profiling_time_min\": 65.5,\n248\t      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n249\t    },\n250\t    \"tables\": [\n251\t      {\n252\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Profiling Resolution Impact (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n253\t        \"rows\": [\n254\t          {\n255\t            \"resolution\": \"Low-res (16×512)\",\n256\t            \"ppl\": 11.23,\n257\t            \"nonzero_heads\": 37,\n258\t            \"time_min\": \"~10\"\n259\t          },\n260\t          {\n261\t            \"resolution\": \"High-res (64×2048)\",\n262\t            \"ppl\": 10.91,\n263\t            \"nonzero_heads\": 100,\n264\t            \"time_min\": 65.5\n265\t          },\n266\t          {\n267\t            \"resolution\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n268\t            \"ppl\": 15.45,\n269\t            \"nonzero_heads\": \"N/A\",\n270\t            \"time_min\": 0\n271\t          }\n272\t        ]\n273\t      }\n274\t    ],\n275\t    \"figures\": [],\n276\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中作为 engineering insight 被接受。Reviewer 不会 object 但建议 放 appendix 而非 main body。对 claim 的影响中性——既不强化也不削弱核心论点。\\n\\n\\n高分辨率 profiling 将 PPL 从 11.23 降到 10.91（-2.8%），说明 profiling resolution  matters。核心改进来自更准确的 sensitivity ranking：hires 发现 100/112 heads 有 非零 2-bit delta（vs lowres 37/112），导致 8 个 head 的 allocation 改变。 Median reviewer 反应分化：(a) 方法 reviewer 认为这说明 \\\"profiling quality drives  results more than solver choice — the real engineering is in the profiler, not MCKP\\\"， 进一步削弱 solver 作为贡献的地位；(b) 系统 reviewer 注意到 65.5 min profiling time  并质疑 \\\"practitioners won't spend an hour profiling a 7B model to save 0.32 PPL\\\"。 需要在 paper 中 trade-off profiling cost vs quality，并论证 lowres 已足够好 （11.23 vs uniform 15.45, 仍有 27.3% improvement）。\\n\"\n277\t  },\n278\t  {\n279\t    \"name\": \"C4 Cross-Dataset Evaluation\",\n280\t    \"description\": \"在 C4 上评估 Qwen2.5-7B（calibrate on WikiText-2, eval on C4; calibrate on C4, eval on WikiText-2）， 验证结果不是 WikiText-2 specific。\\n\",\n281\t    \"results\": {\n282\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n283\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n284\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_delta\": 4.15,\n285\t      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n286\t      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n287\t      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_mckp_ppl\": 20.56,\n288\t      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_uniform_ppl\": 35.42,\n289\t      \"contamination_impact\": 0.034\n290\t    },\n291\t    \"tables\": [\n292\t      {\n293\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Cross-Dataset Calibration Agreement\",\n294\t        \"rows\": [\n295\t          {\n296\t            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n297\t            \"agreement\": \"108/112 (96.4%)\",\n298\t            \"same_domain_ppl\": 11.29,\n299\t            \"cross_domain_ppl\": 20.56\n300\t          },\n301\t          {\n302\t            \"model\": \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n303\t            \"agreement\": \"250/256 (97.7%)\",\n304\t            \"same_domain_ppl\": 8.45,\n305\t            \"cross_domain_ppl\": 8.65\n306\t          },\n307\t          {\n308\t            \"model\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n309\t            \"agreement\": \"247/256 (96.5%)\",\n310\t            \"same_domain_ppl\": 7.16,\n311\t            \"cross_domain_ppl\": 7.19\n312\t          }\n313\t        ]\n314\t      }\n315\t    ],\n316\t    \"figures\": [],\n317\t    \"analysis\": \"三架构的 >96% agreement 是 strong evidence for calibration robustness。 Median reviewer 视为 useful supplementary experiment，不会 object。 建议放 Section 4 或 appendix。\\n\\n\\n96.4% allocation agreement 跨 calibration source 是 positive signal：profiling  的 head sensitivity ranking 对 calibration data 不敏感。Median reviewer 会认可  cross-dataset robustness 但指出：(a) 只在 Qwen 上验证（\\\"is this agreement rate  architecture-dependent?\\\"），(b) 4/112 disagreement heads 的 identity 和影响未讨论， (c) cross-domain PPL（WiKi→C4: 20.56 vs uniform 35.42）虽然 MCKP 仍胜出， 但绝对 PPL 远高于 same-domain（11.29），说明 calibration domain mismatch 仍有成本。 Reviewer 会建议 \\\"report agreement rate on at least one more architecture\\\" 作为 minor revision。已有 llama_c4_cross_dataset（97.7% agreement）和  mistral_c4_cross_dataset（96.5%）数据可以回应。\\n\"\n318\t  },\n319\t  {\n320\t    \"name\": \"RateQuant Greedy Comparison\",\n321\t    \"description\": \"实现 RateQuant 的 greedy Algorithm 1 在 {2,4,8,16} 上，展示 greedy 在 non-consecutive 集合上 suboptimal。\\n\",\n322\t    \"results\": {\n323\t      \"ratequant_greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n324\t      \"mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 36.92,\n325\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n326\t      \"greedy_bit_distribution\": \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\",\n327\t      \"both_worse_than_uniform\": true,\n328\t      \"greedy_better_than_mckp_unconstrained\": true\n329\t    },\n330\t    \"tables\": [\n331\t      {\n332\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Unconstrained Solver Comparison (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n333\t        \"rows\": [\n334\t          {\n335\t            \"solver\": \"RateQuant Greedy (unconstrained)\",\n336\t            \"ppl\": 32.45,\n337\t            \"n_2bit\": 68,\n338\t            \"status\": \"FAIL\"\n339\t          },\n340\t          {\n341\t            \"solver\": \"MCKP (unconstrained)\",\n342\t            \"ppl\": 36.92,\n343\t            \"n_2bit\": \"≥68\",\n344\t            \"status\": \"FAIL\"\n345\t          },\n346\t          {\n347\t            \"solver\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n348\t            \"ppl\": 15.45,\n349\t            \"n_2bit\": 0,\n350\t            \"status\": \"baseline\"\n351\t          }\n352\t        ]\n353\t      }\n354\t    ],\n355\t    \"figures\": [],\n356\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中该实验的价值被 reinterpret：不再是 \\\"MCKP beats greedy\\\"  而是 \\\"both fail without constraint, both succeed with constraint.\\\"  这是 solver equivalence 叙事的第一半证据。Reviewer 认可这个 framing shift。\\n\\n\\n关键发现：两个 solver 在 unconstrained 设置下都 worse than uniform，但 greedy  (32.45) 反而比 MCKP (36.92) 好！这颠覆了 \\\"MCKP is better optimizer\\\" 的叙事。 Median reviewer 会抓住这个点：\\\"if greedy outperforms MCKP unconstrained,  why do you need MCKP at all?\\\" 回应：unconstrained 时两者都失败（compounding）， 差异无意义；constrained 时两者完全一致（Δ=0.0000）——plan_016 的 solver equivalence  证据。但这确实削弱了 MCKP 作为 solver contribution 的叙事，支持 reframe： \\\"constraint is the contribution, not the solver.\\\" 一位 reviewer 会标注  \\\"the unconstrained MCKP being worse than greedy suggests the ILP formulation  interacts poorly with compounding — discuss this.\\\" 需要在 paper 中解释为什么 MCKP 更容易 over-allocate 2-bit（因为它更 aggressively optimizes per-head  cost-benefit，导致更多 2-bit assignments）。\\n\"\n357\t  },\n358\t  {\n359\t    \"name\": \"Oracle Comparison (Subset Brute-Force)\",\n360\t    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 的 3-4 个 layer group 上做 brute-force optimal allocation， 量化 MCKP gap to oracle。\\n\",\n361\t    \"results\": {\n362\t      \"mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n363\t      \"max_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.018,\n364\t      \"avg_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.005,\n365\t      \"layers_mckp_optimal\": \"5/8\",\n366\t      \"layers_with_gap\": 3,\n367\t      \"gap_nature\": \"2-bit head position swap within same bit budget\",\n368\t      \"total_evals\": 54\n369\t    },\n370\t    \"tables\": [\n371\t      {\n372\t        \"caption\": \"Table: MCKP vs Oracle Gap (Qwen2.5-7B, per layer group)\",\n373\t        \"rows\": [\n374\t          {\n375\t            \"layer_group\": \"L0-L3\",\n376\t            \"mckp_optimal\": true,\n377\t            \"gap_ppl\": 0.0\n378\t          },\n379\t          {\n380\t            \"layer_group\": \"L4-L7\",\n381\t            \"mckp_optimal\": false,\n382\t            \"gap_ppl\": 0.0045\n383\t          },\n384\t          {\n385\t            \"layer_group\": \"L8-L11\",\n386\t            \"mckp_optimal\": false,\n387\t            \"gap_ppl\": 0.0136\n388\t          },\n389\t          {\n390\t            \"layer_group\": \"L12-L15\",\n391\t            \"mckp_optimal\": true,\n392\t            \"gap_ppl\": 0.0\n393\t          }\n394\t        ]\n395\t      }\n396\t    ],\n397\t    \"figures\": [],\n398\t    \"analysis\": \"Near-zero oracle gap 与 solver equivalence 共同构成 \\\"constraint is what matters\\\"  的完整论证。Median reviewer 视为 thorough analysis, 建议作为 Section 4 的 supporting evidence。\\n\\n\\nMCKP 与 oracle 的 gap 极小（max 0.018 PPL, avg 0.005 PPL），5/8 layer groups  完全 optimal，3 个 gap 来自同 budget 下 2-bit head 位置互换。Median reviewer  会认可 \\\"MCKP is near-optimal within the constrained feasible set\\\" 但立刻指出： \\\"combined with plan_016 showing greedy=MCKP, this means the constraint defines  the quality — any solver that respects the constraint is near-optimal. The MCKP  formulation adds no value.\\\" 这进一步支持 constraint-as-contribution framing， 但同时使 MCKP 作为 method 贡献更不站得住。reviewer 建议 \\\"present MCKP as the  analysis framework, not the algorithmic contribution.\\\" 在 median 档中这个实验 反而帮助了 reframe——它是 \\\"solver doesn't matter\\\" 叙事的 complementary evidence。\\n\"\n399\t  },\n400\t  {\n401\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Domain Calibration Robustness\",\n402\t    \"description\": \"C4 calibration → WikiText-2 eval 和反方向，报告 per-head allocation agreement rate。\\n\",\n403\t    \"results\": {\n404\t      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n405\t      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n406\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n407\t      \"cross_domain_gap_vs_same_domain\": 0.06\n408\t    },\n409\t    \"tables\": [],\n410\t    \"figures\": [],\n411\t    \"analysis\": \"Minor positive signal。在 median 档中作为 robustness check 被接受， 不影响 overall score。\\n\\n\\n与 plan_007 共享数据。96.4% agreement 说明 profiling-based sensitivity ranking  对 calibration source 高度鲁棒。Median reviewer 反应温和 positive——这是 expected behavior（\\\"if head sensitivity is an architectural property, it shouldn't  depend on calibration data\\\"），所以不会 strongly impress but also won't object。 主要 reviewer concern 是 Qwen-only，但已有三架构数据（Qwen 96.4%, Llama 97.7%,  Mistral 96.5%）可补充。\\n\"\n412\t  },\n413\t  {\n414\t    \"name\": \"Head Sensitivity Visualization\",\n415\t    \"description\": \"生成 per-head profiling delta heatmap、compounding curve、budget allocation 对比图。\\n\",\n416\t    \"results\": {\n417\t      \"figures_generated\": 3,\n418\t      \"heatmap_shows_l0_dominance\": true,\n419\t      \"compounding_curve_elbow\": \"k≈16\",\n420\t      \"allocation_comparison_shows_constraint_effect\": true\n421\t    },\n422\t    \"tables\": [],\n423\t    \"figures\": [],\n424\t    \"analysis\": \"Presentation-level contribution。Median reviewer 可能 suggest 改进但不会 因为 visualization 加分或扣分。\\n\\n\\n可视化是 presentation quality 问题而非科学证据。Median reviewer 会在 minor comments 中评价：\\\"Figure X clearly shows the L0 dominance pattern\\\"  或 \\\"the compounding curve would benefit from error bars.\\\" 不影响 score 但 好的可视化可以帮助 reviewer 快速理解 compounding 现象。关键是 heatmap 要 展示 Qwen（spread, L0 cluster 明显）vs Yi（spike, 单个 L4H3 突出）vs  Gemma-2（flat, 无显著差异）的对比——如果只展示 Qwen，reviewer 会说  \\\"cherry-picked visualization.\\\"\\n\"\n425\t  },\n426\t  {\n427\t    \"name\": \"K/V Separation\",\n428\t    \"description\": \"K 和 V heads 作为独立 MCKP items，独立 budget allocation。与 joint K=V 方法对比。\\n\",\n429\t    \"results\": {\n430\t      \"kv_sep_ppl\": 11.22,\n431\t      \"joint_kv_ppl\": 10.91,\n432\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n433\t      \"delta_sep_vs_joint\": 0.31,\n434\t      \"sep_k_2bit_count\": 16,\n435\t      \"sep_v_uniform_4bit\": true,\n436\t      \"kv_asymmetric_heads\": 21\n437\t    },\n438\t    \"tables\": [\n439\t      {\n440\t        \"caption\": \"Table: K/V Separation vs Joint (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n441\t        \"rows\": [\n442\t          {\n443\t            \"method\": \"Joint K=V (k=8)\",\n444\t            \"ppl\": 10.91,\n445\t            \"k_2bit\": 8,\n446\t            \"v_2bit\": 0\n447\t          },\n448\t          {\n449\t            \"method\": \"K/V Separation\",\n450\t            \"ppl\": 11.22,\n451\t            \"k_2bit\": 16,\n452\t            \"v_2bit\": 0\n453\t          },\n454\t          {\n455\t            \"method\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n456\t            \"ppl\": 15.45,\n457\t            \"k_2bit\": 0,\n458\t            \"v_2bit\": 0\n459\t          }\n460\t        ]\n461\t      }\n462\t    ],\n463\t    \"figures\": [],\n464\t    \"analysis\": \"Negative result 但 informative。在 median 档中被视为 thorough ablation， 可放 appendix。不影响核心 claim。\\n\\n\\nK/V separation 反而 worse（11.22 vs 10.91, +0.31 PPL）。separation 给 K heads  分配了 16 个 2-bit（超过 max_2bit=8 的 joint 约束），导致 K cache compounding。 V heads 在 separation 下全部 4-bit（optimal for V），但 K cache 的退化超过了 V 的收益。Median reviewer 会认为这是 negative result 但有 insight value： \\\"K cache is more sensitive to 2-bit compounding than V — this explains why  joint K=V treatment with a single cardinality constraint works better.\\\"  一位 reviewer 可能 suggest \\\"apply per-cache-type cardinality constraint\\\"  as future work。不会成为 major objection。\\n\"\n465\t  },\n466\t  {\n467\t    \"name\": \"Downstream Task Evaluation (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n468\t    \"description\": \"ARC-C / HellaSwag / PIQA / WinoGrande 在 Qwen2.5-7B 4× 压缩下评估。 验证 PPL improvement 转化为 downstream performance。\\n\",\n469\t    \"results\": {\n470\t      \"arc_c_uniform\": 0.4812,\n471\t      \"arc_c_mckp\": 0.5137,\n472\t      \"arc_c_delta_pp\": 3.16,\n473\t      \"hellaswag_uniform\": 0.7284,\n474\t      \"hellaswag_mckp\": 0.7684,\n475\t      \"hellaswag_delta_pp\": 4.0,\n476\t      \"piqa_uniform\": 0.7661,\n477\t      \"piqa_mckp\": 0.7786,\n478\t      \"piqa_delta_pp\": 1.25,\n479\t      \"winogrande_uniform\": 0.6622,\n480\t      \"winogrande_mckp\": 0.6819,\n481\t      \"winogrande_delta_pp\": 1.97,\n482\t      \"avg_recovery\": 0.728,\n483\t      \"bf16_avg\": 0.688\n484\t    },\n485\t    \"tables\": [\n486\t      {\n487\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Downstream Evaluation — Full Cross-Architecture\",\n488\t        \"rows\": [\n489\t          {\n490\t            \"model\": \"Qwen (Spread)\",\n491\t            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"+2.60\",\n492\t            \"arc_c_delta\": \"+3.16\",\n493\t            \"verdict\": \"Benefit\"\n494\t          },\n495\t          {\n496\t            \"model\": \"Yi-1.5 (Spike)\",\n497\t            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"-0.77\",\n498\t            \"arc_c_delta\": \"-3.24\",\n499\t            \"verdict\": \"Degradation\"\n500\t          },\n501\t          {\n502\t            \"model\": \"Llama (Spike)\",\n503\t            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"-0.99\",\n504\t            \"arc_c_delta\": \"-2.65\",\n505\t            \"verdict\": \"Degradation\"\n506\t          },\n507\t          {\n508\t            \"model\": \"Mistral (Flat)\",\n509\t            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"-0.48\",\n510\t            \"arc_c_delta\": \"-1.19\",\n511\t            \"verdict\": \"Degradation\"\n512\t          },\n513\t          {\n514\t            \"model\": \"Gemma-2 (Flat)\",\n515\t            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"+0.14\",\n516\t            \"arc_c_delta\": \"-0.17\",\n517\t            \"verdict\": \"Noise\"\n518\t          }\n519\t        ]\n520\t      }\n521\t    ],\n522\t    \"figures\": [],\n523\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中这是 double-edged evidence。Qwen 的 downstream gains 被认可但 限定为 \\\"architecture-specific\\\"。跨架构 degradation 要求论文措辞从 \\\"non-uniform improves downstream\\\" 改为 \\\"non-uniform allocation improves downstream  performance specifically on architectures with spread sensitivity patterns (1/5  tested); on other architectures, uniform 4-bit should be preferred.\\\"  arc_challenge 系统性退化需要主动讨论段落。\\n\\n\\nQwen downstream gains 一致 positive（+1.25 to +4.00pp），与 PPL improvement  方向一致。但 median reviewer 的核心 objection 是 A4：\\\"this only works on Qwen.\\\" 跨架构 downstream 数据显示 Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp,  Gemma-2 +0.14pp（noise）。reviewer 会写：\\\"4/5 architectures show negative or  negligible downstream effect. The method degrades downstream performance on most  models.\\\" 另一个 median-specific concern 是 lack of multi-seed CI：3.16pp arc_c  delta 没有 confidence interval，\\\"could be within single-run variance\\\"（A6）。 已有 qwen_3seed_downstream_ci（arc_c std=0.0035, hellaswag std=0.0022） 可部分回应。arc_challenge 跨模型系统性退化（Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp,  Mistral -1.19pp）会被特别标注——reviewer 要求主动讨论这个 pattern。\\n\"\n524\t  },\n525\t  {\n526\t    \"name\": \"70B Profiling-Only\",\n527\t    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-72B 上做 distortion profiling（不做 full eval），分析 sensitivity  patterns 是否随模型大小 scale。\\n\",\n528\t    \"results\": {\n529\t      \"status\": \"killed\",\n530\t      \"sensitivity_pattern_observed\": null,\n531\t      \"l0_dominance_scales\": null\n532\t    },\n533\t    \"tables\": [],\n534\t    \"figures\": [],\n535\t    \"analysis\": \"Missing data。Median reviewer 标注为 limitation，不作为 reject reason。\\n\\n\\n实验被 killed（可能 OOM 或 timeout）。Median reviewer 会注意到 \\\"only 7B-14B  scale models tested\\\" 并标注为 limitation：\\\"no evidence that findings generalize  to production-scale models (70B+).\\\" 但在 median 档中这是 minor gap 而非 major  objection——大多数 KV cache quantization papers 也只测 7B-14B。缺少 70B 数据 会降低 \\\"practical implications\\\" 的说服力但不会导致 reject。建议在 limitations  中明确承认 \\\"our experiments are limited to 7B-14B scale; scaling behavior of  compounding effects to 70B+ models remains an open question.\\\"\\n\"\n536\t  },\n537\t  {\n538\t    \"name\": \"L0-Only Heuristic Baseline\",\n539\t    \"description\": \"最简单的 non-uniform 策略：L0 heads 8-bit，其余 uniform 4-bit。如果 L0-only 匹配 MCKP，full optimization 不必要。\\n\",\n540\t    \"results\": {\n541\t      \"qwen_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n542\t      \"qwen_l0_random_mean\": 11.69,\n543\t      \"qwen_l0_random_std\": 0.47,\n544\t      \"qwen_l0_random_median\": 11.52,\n545\t      \"qwen_naive_positional_ppl\": 12.23,\n546\t      \"llama_mckp_ppl\": 8.45,\n547\t      \"llama_l0_random_mean\": 10.48,\n548\t      \"llama_naive_positional\": 9.94,\n549\t      \"mistral_mckp_ppl\": 7.16,\n550\t      \"mistral_l0_random_mean\": 7.56,\n551\t      \"mistral_naive_positional\": 7.48,\n552\t      \"mckp_consistently_beats_l0_random\": true\n553\t    },\n554\t    \"tables\": [\n555\t      {\n556\t        \"caption\": \"Table: MCKP vs Heuristic Baselines (budget=0.25)\",\n557\t        \"rows\": [\n558\t          {\n559\t            \"model\": \"Qwen\",\n560\t            \"mckp\": 10.91,\n561\t            \"l0_random_median\": 11.52,\n562\t            \"naive_positional\": 12.23,\n563\t            \"uniform\": 15.45\n564\t          },\n565\t          {\n566\t            \"model\": \"Llama\",\n567\t            \"mckp\": 8.45,\n568\t            \"l0_random_median\": 10.04,\n569\t            \"naive_positional\": 9.94,\n570\t            \"uniform\": 8.47\n571\t          },\n572\t          {\n573\t            \"model\": \"Mistral\",\n574\t            \"mckp\": 7.16,\n575\t            \"l0_random_median\": 7.59,\n576\t            \"naive_positional\": 7.48,\n577\t            \"uniform\": 7.13\n578\t          }\n579\t        ]\n580\t      }\n581\t    ],\n582\t    \"figures\": [],\n583\t    \"analysis\": \"Median reviewer 认为这是 critical missing baseline 被补充后的 adequate response。 MCKP vs L0-random gap（5-16%）证明 solver 在 constraint-respecting 方案中仍有 optimization 价值。但 Mistral 的 MCKP(7.16) > uniform(7.13) 再次说明 flat  architecture 上任何 non-uniform 都是 net negative。\\n\\n\\nL0-only heuristic 的 PPL（Qwen median 11.52, mean 11.69）consistently worse  than MCKP（10.91），差距 -5.2%。这说明 profiling-based allocation 在 constraint  内仍有 optimization value——不仅仅是 \\\"protect L0 and done.\\\" Median reviewer  反应正面但有 nuance：(a) \\\"MCKP beats L0-random by 5.2% — meaningful but not  dramatic. The naive positional heuristic (12.23) is much worse, so profiling does  matter.\\\" (b) \\\"seed variance in L0-random is large (std=0.47, range 11.33-12.52),  suggesting the specific choice of which non-L0 heads get 2-bit matters significantly.\\\"  (c) Llama 和 Mistral 上 MCKP vs L0-random gap 更大（Llama: 8.45 vs 10.04 median,  -15.8%），说明 even on non-benefit architectures, random constraint-respecting  allocation is much worse than MCKP — the solver finds better allocations even when  the absolute PPL difference vs uniform is small. 这个 experiment 的原始设计被 kill 但后来用 corrected version (l0_heuristic_corrected) 完成。\\n\"\n584\t  },\n585\t  {\n586\t    \"name\": \"Greedy + Cardinality Constraint Ablation (Solver Equivalence)\",\n587\t    \"description\": \"RateQuant greedy + max_2bit=k 约束。对比 (a) greedy unconstrained,  (b) greedy constrained k=8, (c) MCKP constrained k=8。\\n\",\n588\t    \"results\": {\n589\t      \"greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n590\t      \"greedy_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n591\t      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n592\t      \"delta_greedy_vs_mckp_constrained\": 0.0012,\n593\t      \"bit_distribution_identical\": true,\n594\t      \"distribution\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n595\t    },\n596\t    \"tables\": [\n597\t      {\n598\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Solver Equivalence Under Constraint (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n599\t        \"rows\": [\n600\t          {\n601\t            \"solver\": \"Greedy unconstrained\",\n602\t            \"ppl\": 32.45,\n603\t            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\",\n604\t            \"status\": \"FAIL\"\n605\t          },\n606\t          {\n607\t            \"solver\": \"Greedy + max_2bit=8\",\n608\t            \"ppl\": 11.23,\n609\t            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\",\n610\t            \"status\": \"PASS\"\n611\t          },\n612\t          {\n613\t            \"solver\": \"MCKP + max_2bit=8\",\n614\t            \"ppl\": 11.23,\n615\t            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\",\n616\t            \"status\": \"PASS\"\n617\t          },\n618\t          {\n619\t            \"solver\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n620\t            \"ppl\": 15.45,\n621\t            \"bit_dist\": \"all 4-bit\",\n622\t            \"status\": \"baseline\"\n623\t          }\n624\t        ]\n625\t      }\n626\t    ],\n627\t    \"figures\": [],\n628\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中被认可为 paper 的 highlight。两位 reviewer 会引用此结果支持 \\\"the constraint is the contribution\\\" narrative。但第三位 reviewer 用此结果 反驳 \\\"then what exactly is the technical contribution — discovering that you need  a max_2bit cap? That's a hyperparameter, not a method.\\\"\\n\\n\\n这是 paper 最 powerful 的单个实验：constrained greedy = constrained MCKP  (Δ=0.0012 PPL, identical bit distribution)。证明 constraint 是唯一 intervention  that matters——两个算法复杂度完全不同的 solver 在 constraint 下产生相同解。 Median reviewer 对此实验的反应最 positive：\\\"this is the strongest evidence in the  paper — it shows the cardinality constraint is the real contribution, not the  optimization algorithm.\\\" 但也引发 A3 concern：\\\"if a simple cardinality constraint  is all you need, this is essentially one hyperparameter — is that a sufficient  contribution for a main conference paper?\\\" Reviewer 会要求 (a) 更强的 principled  justification for why cardinality constraint works（不只是 empirical observation）， (b) 讨论 constraint 与 RateQuant 的 distortion model 的关系。Qwen14b 上也验证了 solver equivalence（greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0），增加了 generality。\\n\"\n629\t  },\n630\t  {\n631\t    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Error Bars\",\n632\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B 上 3 个不同 calibration seed 的 constrained MCKP，报告 mean±std。\\n\",\n633\t    \"results\": {\n634\t      \"mckp_seed0\": 11.02,\n635\t      \"mckp_seed1\": 10.9,\n636\t      \"mckp_seed2\": 11.05,\n637\t      \"mckp_mean\": 10.99,\n638\t      \"mckp_std\": 0.065,\n639\t      \"bit_dist_all_seeds\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\",\n640\t      \"allocation_agreement_3way\": 0.902,\n641\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n642\t      \"improvement_significant\": true,\n643\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 11.12,\n644\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 10.86\n645\t    },\n646\t    \"tables\": [\n647\t      {\n648\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Multi-Seed PPL Stability (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n649\t        \"rows\": [\n650\t          {\n651\t            \"seed\": 0,\n652\t            \"ppl\": 11.02,\n653\t            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n654\t          },\n655\t          {\n656\t            \"seed\": 1,\n657\t            \"ppl\": 10.9,\n658\t            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n659\t          },\n660\t          {\n661\t            \"seed\": 2,\n662\t            \"ppl\": 11.05,\n663\t            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n664\t          },\n665\t          {\n666\t            \"seed\": \"mean±std\",\n667\t            \"ppl\": \"10.99±0.065\",\n668\t            \"bit_dist\": \"consistent\"\n669\t          }\n670\t        ]\n671\t      }\n672\t    ],\n673\t    \"figures\": [],\n674\t    \"analysis\": \"Median reviewer 接受 PPL 层面的 statistical credibility 但要求 downstream CI。 这是 median 档的 typical gap——不至于 reject 但会是 \\\"requested revision\\\" 的一部分。\\n\\n\\nstd=0.065 意味着 95% CI 约 [10.86, 11.12]，远低于 uniform 15.45——improvement  统计上 robust。Bit distribution 在所有 seed 下一致（{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}）， allocation agreement 90.2% 跨 seed。Median reviewer 会认可 PPL stability 但有 两个 residual concerns：(a) \\\"3 seeds is the minimum — 5 seeds with proper CI would  be more convincing\\\"（minor revision level），(b) \\\"allocation agreement 90.2% means  10% of heads flip between seeds — which heads and how does it affect downstream?\\\"  更严重的是 A6：**缺少 multi-seed downstream CI**。PPL multi-seed 已有，但  downstream 的 arc_c +3.16pp 没有 error bar。qwen_3seed_downstream_ci 提供了 部分数据（arc_c std=0.0035），但只在 Qwen 上。Reviewer 会标注 \\\"multi-seed  downstream CI missing for non-Qwen architectures\\\" 作为 significant gap。\\n\"\n675\t  },\n676\t  {\n677\t    \"name\": \"Runtime/Latency Benchmark\",\n678\t    \"description\": \"End-to-end inference latency 和 throughput，mixed-precision KV cache vs uniform 4-bit。\\n\",\n679\t    \"results\": {\n680\t      \"bf16_prefill_ms\": 45.86,\n681\t      \"bf16_decode_ms\": 33.78,\n682\t      \"bf16_throughput\": 29.6,\n683\t      \"uniform4_prefill_ms\": 54.25,\n684\t      \"uniform4_decode_ms\": 42.46,\n685\t      \"uniform4_throughput\": 23.6,\n686\t      \"mckp_prefill_ms\": 57.03,\n687\t      \"mckp_decode_ms\": 46.09,\n688\t      \"mckp_throughput\": 21.8,\n689\t      \"mckp_solver_time_sec\": 0.005,\n690\t      \"memory_compression_4x\": true,\n691\t      \"mckp_overhead_vs_uniform_pct\": 8.5,\n692\t      \"mckp_overhead_vs_bf16_pct\": 36.4\n693\t    },\n694\t    \"tables\": [\n695\t      {\n696\t        \"caption\": \"Table: Runtime Benchmark (Qwen2.5-7B, seq_len=2048)\",\n697\t        \"rows\": [\n698\t          {\n699\t            \"method\": \"BF16 (no quantization)\",\n700\t            \"prefill_ms\": 45.86,\n701\t            \"decode_ms\": 33.78,\n702\t            \"throughput\": 29.6,\n703\t            \"memory_MB\": 21\n704\t          },\n705\t          {\n706\t            \"method\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n707\t            \"prefill_ms\": 54.25,\n708\t            \"decode_ms\": 42.46,\n709\t            \"throughput\": 23.6,\n710\t            \"memory_MB\": 5.25\n711\t          },\n712\t          {\n713\t            \"method\": \"Constrained MCKP\",\n714\t            \"prefill_ms\": 57.03,\n715\t            \"decode_ms\": 46.09,\n716\t            \"throughput\": 21.8,\n717\t            \"memory_MB\": 5.25\n718\t          }\n719\t        ]\n720\t      }\n721\t    ],\n722\t    \"figures\": [],\n723\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中这是 second major objection source。Runtime overhead 与  \\\"practical implications\\\" claim 冲突。Paper 需要 reframe：\\\"memory-bound  scenarios (long context, large batch) where 4× memory reduction enables  deployment that bf16 cannot.\\\" 8K context 实验（qwen7b_8k_context_eval:  uniform 77.75 vs MCKP 8.59）是 strongest counterargument——at long context,  memory savings dominate and quality gap amplifies dramatically。\\n\\n令人意外的 negative finding：mixed-precision MCKP 比 uniform 4-bit 更慢 （throughput 21.8 vs 23.6 tok/s, -7.6%），甚至比 bf16 baseline 更慢 （21.8 vs 29.6 tok/s, -26.4%）。原因是 mixed-precision 需要 per-head 不同 的 dequantization kernel，当前实现缺少 fused kernel optimization。 Median reviewer 反应强烈 negative：\\\"the method provides 29% PPL improvement  on Qwen but costs 8% throughput — practitioners would need to decide if PPL  improvement justifies speed regression. On 7/8 architectures where there's no  PPL benefit, the speed cost is pure overhead.\\\" 这成为 major objection 之一（A6  范畴）。MCKP solver 本身只需 0.005s（negligible），所以 overhead 完全来自 inference-time mixed-precision dequantization。需要在 paper 中承认 \\\"current  implementation uses naive per-head dequantization; a fused kernel could eliminate  the overhead\\\" 并标注为 engineering limitation, not fundamental。但 reviewer 会 counter：\\\"without the optimized kernel, the practical benefit claim is weakened.\\\"\\n\"\n724\t  }\n725\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc8fbc02-a351-42eb-9162-8abd7e156f3e","uuid":"3405a85b-9e28-46a6-afe5-cd44efbe7d57","timestamp":"2026-05-16T02:37:22.152Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/ratekv/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T021448/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"L0 Exclusion Removal Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"移除 L0 排除约束，仅保留 max_2bit=8，验证 solver 纯粹从 profiling data 自动发现 L0 敏感结构。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"solver_auto_assigns_8bit_to_L0\": true,\n      \"ppl_without_l0_exclusion\": 10.91,\n      \"ppl_with_l0_exclusion\": 10.91,\n      \"delta\": 0.0,\n      \"l0_heads_assigned_8bit\": 4,\n      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: L0 Exclusion Ablation (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"MCKP + L0 exclusion + max_2bit=8\",\n            \"ppl\": 10.91,\n            \"l0_bit\": \"8-bit (hard-coded)\",\n            \"note\": \"原始设置\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"MCKP + max_2bit=8 only\",\n            \"ppl\": 10.91,\n            \"l0_bit\": \"8-bit (solver-discovered)\",\n            \"note\": \"solver 自动分配\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 评价：supportive but minor。在 median 档中被视为 completeness ablation  而非核心证据。reviewer 可能建议移到 appendix。不影响主要 claim 但增加 paper 完整性。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下该结果被 reviewer 认可为 neat ablation——solver 自动发现 L0 是最敏感的层， 不需要手动排除。但 reviewer 会指出这只在 Qwen 上验证（L0 dominance ratio=26×）， 对于 L0 dominance 低的架构（Yi 0.07，Mistral 1.74）solver 是否同样能自动发现正确结构 缺少验证。一位 reviewer 可能注释 \\\"this is expected — L0 has the largest profiling delta  by far, so any reasonable solver would protect it.\\\" 不会成为主要 objection，但也不会 被视为独立贡献。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B Full Pipeline Replication\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Llama-3.1-8B（GQA 4:1）上复制完整 pipeline——profiling、constrained MCKP、PPL 评估。 测试跨架构泛化性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 8.09,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 8.47,\n      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 8.45,\n      \"delta_vs_uniform_pct\": 0.2,\n      \"delta_vs_uniform_ppl\": 0.02,\n      \"memory_ratio\": 0.25,\n      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:2, 4:253, 8:1}\",\n      \"natural_2bit_count\": 2,\n      \"constraint_binds\": false,\n      \"unconstrained_degradation_ratio\": 1.07,\n      \"top5_concentration\": 0.57,\n      \"distribution_shape\": \"Spike\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Llama-3.1-8B Pipeline Results (budget=0.25)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"BF16 baseline\",\n            \"ppl\": 8.09,\n            \"bits\": \"16\",\n            \"note\": \"\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            \"ppl\": 8.47,\n            \"bits\": \"4.0\",\n            \"note\": \"\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Unconstrained MCKP\",\n            \"ppl\": 8.63,\n            \"bits\": \"mixed\",\n            \"note\": \"1.07× baseline\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Constrained MCKP (k=8)\",\n            \"ppl\": 8.45,\n            \"bits\": \"{2:2, 4:253, 8:1}\",\n            \"note\": \"+0.2% vs uniform\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median reviewer 会同时肯定和批评：肯定 honest reporting of negative result， 批评 \\\"if 7/8 architectures show no benefit, this is not a method paper — it's an  analysis paper that happens to find one architecture where optimization helps.\\\"  这强化了 reframe 为 empirical analysis 的需要。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，Llama 的 marginal 结果（+0.2% vs uniform）成为 reviewer 攻击点之一。 reviewer 会写 \\\"the method provides essentially no benefit on Llama — the +0.2%  improvement is within noise.\\\" Llama 的 spike distribution（L2H5 单个 outlier 主导， t₁/t₅≈0.85）导致 solver 只选择 2 个 head 做 2-bit，constraint 从不触发（natural k=2 < max_2bit=8）， MCKP 优化空间极小。这解释了为什么 PPL 差异几乎为零。但从 compounding 角度， unconstrained 仍然 1.07× baseline，说明即使 mild 情况下 solver 仍会略微 over-allocate。 Reviewer 会要求诚实报告 \\\"no benefit\\\" 而非 spin 为 positive。在 median 档中， 这个 negative result 本身不被反对——reviewer 反对的是用 8 个架构中只有 1 个 positive  来声称 method 有效。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 Full Pipeline Replication\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Mistral-7B-v0.3 上复制完整 pipeline。不同架构家族，建立跨架构有效性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 7.035,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 7.131,\n      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 7.165,\n      \"delta_vs_uniform_pct\": -0.5,\n      \"delta_vs_uniform_ppl\": -0.034,\n      \"memory_ratio\": 0.25,\n      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:4, 4:252}\",\n      \"unconstrained_degradation_ratio\": 1.08,\n      \"top5_concentration\": 0.22,\n      \"distribution_shape\": \"Flat\",\n      \"k_ablation_monotonic\": true,\n      \"best_k_still_worse_than_uniform\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Mistral-7B-v0.3 k-Ablation (budget=0.25)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"k\": 4,\n            \"ppl\": 7.165,\n            \"n_2bit\": 4,\n            \"note\": \"best constrained, still > uniform\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"k\": 8,\n            \"ppl\": 7.2,\n            \"n_2bit\": 8,\n            \"note\": \"\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"k\": 16,\n            \"ppl\": 7.311,\n            \"n_2bit\": 16,\n            \"note\": \"\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"k\": \"uniform\",\n            \"ppl\": 7.131,\n            \"n_2bit\": 0,\n            \"note\": \"optimal for Mistral\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在 median 档中，Mistral negative result 既是弱点也是优势。弱点：method 不 work。 优势：honest negative result 增加 credibility，且支持 diagnostic 的必要性—— 如果没有 diagnostic，practitioners 会浪费 profiling 时间在 Mistral 这样的模型上。 Reviewer 2 (偏方法) 会将此作为 \\\"method only works on Qwen\\\" 的证据。 Reviewer 3 (偏分析) 会认可这增加了 paper 的科学价值。\\n\\n\\nMistral 是最强 negative case：MCKP 在所有 k 值下都 worse than uniform。 PPL 随 k 单调递增（k=4: 7.165, k=8: 7.200, k=18: 7.323），profiler 报告近零  sensitivity 差异（concentration=0.22, CV=1.31）。这表明 Mistral 的 KV head  sensitivity 高度均匀——没有 head 从 2-bit downgrade 中获益。Median reviewer  会将此视为 \\\"method failure on flat architectures\\\" 和 \\\"proof that uniform 4-bit  is optimal when profiler gives zero signal.\\\" 对 compounding claim 仍有帮助： unconstrained 1.08× 表明即使 flat distribution，solver 仍 over-allocate  2-bit heads（42/256=16.4%）。但 reviewer 会质疑 \\\"1.08× is hardly catastrophic  — this is within the range where a practitioner wouldn't even notice.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Compounding Effect Characterization Sweep\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上扫 max_2bit 从 0 到 112，绘制 PPL vs max_2bit 曲线， 确定 compounding 阈值。建立 cardinality constraint 的 principled 基础。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"k0_ppl\": 9.81,\n      \"k8_ppl\": 10.05,\n      \"k16_ppl\": 10.42,\n      \"k32_ppl\": 11.6,\n      \"k64_ppl\": 23.22,\n      \"k112_ppl\": 98.75,\n      \"compounding_threshold_k\": 16,\n      \"max_compounding_ratio\": 10.07,\n      \"curve_shape\": \"superlinear after k≈16, exponential after k≈48\",\n      \"safe_k_range\": \"k≤8 universally <2.5% degradation\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Compounding Sweep (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"k\": 0,\n            \"ppl\": 9.81,\n            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"1.00×\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"k\": 8,\n            \"ppl\": 10.05,\n            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"1.02×\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"k\": 16,\n            \"ppl\": 10.42,\n            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"1.06×\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"k\": 32,\n            \"ppl\": 11.6,\n            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"1.18×\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"k\": 64,\n            \"ppl\": 23.22,\n            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"2.37×\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"k\": 112,\n            \"ppl\": 98.75,\n            \"ratio_to_baseline\": \"10.07×\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median reviewer 的核心反馈：compounding effect 是 real and well-characterized， 但 novelty 因 RateQuant Appendix M 打折。建议在 related work 中显式讨论  \\\"RateQuant acknowledges compounding in Appendix M but does not characterize the  threshold or provide a fix — our sweep provides the first quantitative mapping.\\\"  三架构对比增加说服力：Qwen 的 U-shape（optimal k=8）、Llama 的 flat profile （natural k=2, constraint irrelevant）、Mistral 的 monotonic increase（every  2-bit head hurts）展示了 architecture-dependent compounding behavior。\\n\\n\\nCompounding sweep 是 median 档中最被认可的实验——提供了 compounding 效应的 定量证据。PPL 在 k≤8 时近线性增长（9.81→10.05, +2.4%），k=16-32 开始加速 （10.42→11.60），k≥48 后指数爆炸（23.22→98.75）。这条曲线是 \\\"principled  basis for constraint selection\\\" 的核心证据。但 median reviewer 会有两个质疑： (1) \\\"这条曲线只在 Qwen 上做了——其他架构的阈值可能完全不同\\\"（A2）， (2) \\\"RateQuant Appendix M 已经 acknowledge compounding，这个 sweep 只是 quantified 了已知现象\\\"（A1）。需要补充 Llama 和 Mistral 的 compounding sweep  来部分 address (1)——实际已有数据（llama_compounding_sweep, mistral_compounding_sweep_v2） 可以回应。Reviewer 对 k≤8 safety 的 claim 会接受，但会要求去掉 \\\"universally safe\\\"  改为 \\\"safe across all tested architectures.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Budget Sweep (2×/4×/8× Compression)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上测试 2×/4×/8× 压缩比下的 constrained MCKP vs uniform baseline。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"budget_0.5_mckp_ppl\": 9.85,\n      \"budget_0.5_uniform_ppl\": 9.86,\n      \"budget_0.5_delta_pct\": 0.1,\n      \"budget_0.25_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"budget_0.25_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"budget_0.25_delta_pct\": 29.4,\n      \"budget_0.125_mckp_ppl\": 57.6,\n      \"budget_0.125_uniform_2bit_ppl\": 2643.77,\n      \"budget_0.125_delta_ratio\": \"45.9×\",\n      \"compression_amplifies_benefit\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Budget Sweep (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"compression\": \"2× (budget=0.5)\",\n            \"mckp_ppl\": 9.85,\n            \"uniform_ppl\": 9.86,\n            \"delta\": \"~0%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"compression\": \"4× (budget=0.25)\",\n            \"mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n            \"uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n            \"delta\": \"29.4%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"compression\": \"8× (budget=0.125)\",\n            \"mckp_ppl\": 57.6,\n            \"uniform_ppl\": 2643.77,\n            \"delta\": \"45.9×\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中被部分接受。Reviewer 认可 practical implication（高压缩比下 constraint  essential），但质疑 moderate compression（主要应用场景）下只有 Qwen 获益的泛化性。 建议补充 Llama/Mistral 的 budget sweep 至少在 8× 压缩点。\\n\\n\\nBudget sweep 展示了核心趋势：压缩越激进，constrained MCKP vs uniform 的差距越大。 在 2× 压缩下差异几乎为零（都接近 baseline），4× 时 MCKP 优势 29.4%，8× 时 MCKP 57.60 vs uniform 2643.77（45×差距）。Median reviewer 会认可 aggressive  compression 的 practical value（\\\"at 8× compression, the constraint is the difference  between usable and unusable\\\"），但会指出：(a) 2× 结果说明 moderate compression 下 benefit 主要来自 Qwen 的 spread pattern 而非 method 本身，(b) 8× 的 PPL=57.60  虽远好于 2643.77，但 absolute 值仍然很高——\\\"is a 57.60 PPL model actually usable?\\\"  需要补充 aggressive compression 下的 downstream task 评估。(c) 只在 Qwen 上做了 full sweep，Llama 的 aggressive compression 数据（57.60 vs 2643.77）虽有但 仅一个点，不是 sweep。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"High-Resolution Profiling\",\n    \"description\": \"64 seq × 2048 tokens 的高分辨率 profiling（vs 16×512），验证更好的 profiling  是否改善 solver allocation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hires_constrained_ppl_bf16\": 10.91,\n      \"lowres_constrained_ppl_bf16\": 11.23,\n      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 9.81,\n      \"improvement_vs_lowres\": 0.32,\n      \"improvement_pct\": 2.8,\n      \"hires_nonzero_2bit_heads\": 100,\n      \"lowres_nonzero_2bit_heads\": 37,\n      \"allocation_diff_count\": 8,\n      \"profiling_time_min\": 65.5,\n      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Profiling Resolution Impact (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"resolution\": \"Low-res (16×512)\",\n            \"ppl\": 11.23,\n            \"nonzero_heads\": 37,\n            \"time_min\": \"~10\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"resolution\": \"High-res (64×2048)\",\n            \"ppl\": 10.91,\n            \"nonzero_heads\": 100,\n            \"time_min\": 65.5\n          },\n          {\n            \"resolution\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            \"ppl\": 15.45,\n            \"nonzero_heads\": \"N/A\",\n            \"time_min\": 0\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中作为 engineering insight 被接受。Reviewer 不会 object 但建议 放 appendix 而非 main body。对 claim 的影响中性——既不强化也不削弱核心论点。\\n\\n\\n高分辨率 profiling 将 PPL 从 11.23 降到 10.91（-2.8%），说明 profiling resolution  matters。核心改进来自更准确的 sensitivity ranking：hires 发现 100/112 heads 有 非零 2-bit delta（vs lowres 37/112），导致 8 个 head 的 allocation 改变。 Median reviewer 反应分化：(a) 方法 reviewer 认为这说明 \\\"profiling quality drives  results more than solver choice — the real engineering is in the profiler, not MCKP\\\"， 进一步削弱 solver 作为贡献的地位；(b) 系统 reviewer 注意到 65.5 min profiling time  并质疑 \\\"practitioners won't spend an hour profiling a 7B model to save 0.32 PPL\\\"。 需要在 paper 中 trade-off profiling cost vs quality，并论证 lowres 已足够好 （11.23 vs uniform 15.45, 仍有 27.3% improvement）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"C4 Cross-Dataset Evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"在 C4 上评估 Qwen2.5-7B（calibrate on WikiText-2, eval on C4; calibrate on C4, eval on WikiText-2）， 验证结果不是 WikiText-2 specific。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_delta\": 4.15,\n      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_mckp_ppl\": 20.56,\n      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_uniform_ppl\": 35.42,\n      \"contamination_impact\": 0.034\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Cross-Dataset Calibration Agreement\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen2.5-7B\",\n            \"agreement\": \"108/112 (96.4%)\",\n            \"same_domain_ppl\": 11.29,\n            \"cross_domain_ppl\": 20.56\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            \"agreement\": \"250/256 (97.7%)\",\n            \"same_domain_ppl\": 8.45,\n            \"cross_domain_ppl\": 8.65\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n            \"agreement\": \"247/256 (96.5%)\",\n            \"same_domain_ppl\": 7.16,\n            \"cross_domain_ppl\": 7.19\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三架构的 >96% agreement 是 strong evidence for calibration robustness。 Median reviewer 视为 useful supplementary experiment，不会 object。 建议放 Section 4 或 appendix。\\n\\n\\n96.4% allocation agreement 跨 calibration source 是 positive signal：profiling  的 head sensitivity ranking 对 calibration data 不敏感。Median reviewer 会认可  cross-dataset robustness 但指出：(a) 只在 Qwen 上验证（\\\"is this agreement rate  architecture-dependent?\\\"），(b) 4/112 disagreement heads 的 identity 和影响未讨论， (c) cross-domain PPL（WiKi→C4: 20.56 vs uniform 35.42）虽然 MCKP 仍胜出， 但绝对 PPL 远高于 same-domain（11.29），说明 calibration domain mismatch 仍有成本。 Reviewer 会建议 \\\"report agreement rate on at least one more architecture\\\" 作为 minor revision。已有 llama_c4_cross_dataset（97.7% agreement）和  mistral_c4_cross_dataset（96.5%）数据可以回应。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RateQuant Greedy Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 RateQuant 的 greedy Algorithm 1 在 {2,4,8,16} 上，展示 greedy 在 non-consecutive 集合上 suboptimal。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ratequant_greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n      \"mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 36.92,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"greedy_bit_distribution\": \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\",\n      \"both_worse_than_uniform\": true,\n      \"greedy_better_than_mckp_unconstrained\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Unconstrained Solver Comparison (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"solver\": \"RateQuant Greedy (unconstrained)\",\n            \"ppl\": 32.45,\n            \"n_2bit\": 68,\n            \"status\": \"FAIL\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"solver\": \"MCKP (unconstrained)\",\n            \"ppl\": 36.92,\n            \"n_2bit\": \"≥68\",\n            \"status\": \"FAIL\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"solver\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            \"ppl\": 15.45,\n            \"n_2bit\": 0,\n            \"status\": \"baseline\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中该实验的价值被 reinterpret：不再是 \\\"MCKP beats greedy\\\"  而是 \\\"both fail without constraint, both succeed with constraint.\\\"  这是 solver equivalence 叙事的第一半证据。Reviewer 认可这个 framing shift。\\n\\n\\n关键发现：两个 solver 在 unconstrained 设置下都 worse than uniform，但 greedy  (32.45) 反而比 MCKP (36.92) 好！这颠覆了 \\\"MCKP is better optimizer\\\" 的叙事。 Median reviewer 会抓住这个点：\\\"if greedy outperforms MCKP unconstrained,  why do you need MCKP at all?\\\" 回应：unconstrained 时两者都失败（compounding）， 差异无意义；constrained 时两者完全一致（Δ=0.0000）——plan_016 的 solver equivalence  证据。但这确实削弱了 MCKP 作为 solver contribution 的叙事，支持 reframe： \\\"constraint is the contribution, not the solver.\\\" 一位 reviewer 会标注  \\\"the unconstrained MCKP being worse than greedy suggests the ILP formulation  interacts poorly with compounding — discuss this.\\\" 需要在 paper 中解释为什么 MCKP 更容易 over-allocate 2-bit（因为它更 aggressively optimizes per-head  cost-benefit，导致更多 2-bit assignments）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Oracle Comparison (Subset Brute-Force)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 的 3-4 个 layer group 上做 brute-force optimal allocation， 量化 MCKP gap to oracle。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"max_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.018,\n      \"avg_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.005,\n      \"layers_mckp_optimal\": \"5/8\",\n      \"layers_with_gap\": 3,\n      \"gap_nature\": \"2-bit head position swap within same bit budget\",\n      \"total_evals\": 54\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: MCKP vs Oracle Gap (Qwen2.5-7B, per layer group)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"layer_group\": \"L0-L3\",\n            \"mckp_optimal\": true,\n            \"gap_ppl\": 0.0\n          },\n          {\n            \"layer_group\": \"L4-L7\",\n            \"mckp_optimal\": false,\n            \"gap_ppl\": 0.0045\n          },\n          {\n            \"layer_group\": \"L8-L11\",\n            \"mckp_optimal\": false,\n            \"gap_ppl\": 0.0136\n          },\n          {\n            \"layer_group\": \"L12-L15\",\n            \"mckp_optimal\": true,\n            \"gap_ppl\": 0.0\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Near-zero oracle gap 与 solver equivalence 共同构成 \\\"constraint is what matters\\\"  的完整论证。Median reviewer 视为 thorough analysis, 建议作为 Section 4 的 supporting evidence。\\n\\n\\nMCKP 与 oracle 的 gap 极小（max 0.018 PPL, avg 0.005 PPL），5/8 layer groups  完全 optimal，3 个 gap 来自同 budget 下 2-bit head 位置互换。Median reviewer  会认可 \\\"MCKP is near-optimal within the constrained feasible set\\\" 但立刻指出： \\\"combined with plan_016 showing greedy=MCKP, this means the constraint defines  the quality — any solver that respects the constraint is near-optimal. The MCKP  formulation adds no value.\\\" 这进一步支持 constraint-as-contribution framing， 但同时使 MCKP 作为 method 贡献更不站得住。reviewer 建议 \\\"present MCKP as the  analysis framework, not the algorithmic contribution.\\\" 在 median 档中这个实验 反而帮助了 reframe——它是 \\\"solver doesn't matter\\\" 叙事的 complementary evidence。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Domain Calibration Robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"C4 calibration → WikiText-2 eval 和反方向，报告 per-head allocation agreement rate。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n      \"cross_domain_gap_vs_same_domain\": 0.06\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Minor positive signal。在 median 档中作为 robustness check 被接受， 不影响 overall score。\\n\\n\\n与 plan_007 共享数据。96.4% agreement 说明 profiling-based sensitivity ranking  对 calibration source 高度鲁棒。Median reviewer 反应温和 positive——这是 expected behavior（\\\"if head sensitivity is an architectural property, it shouldn't  depend on calibration data\\\"），所以不会 strongly impress but also won't object。 主要 reviewer concern 是 Qwen-only，但已有三架构数据（Qwen 96.4%, Llama 97.7%,  Mistral 96.5%）可补充。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Head Sensitivity Visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"生成 per-head profiling delta heatmap、compounding curve、budget allocation 对比图。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"figures_generated\": 3,\n      \"heatmap_shows_l0_dominance\": true,\n      \"compounding_curve_elbow\": \"k≈16\",\n      \"allocation_comparison_shows_constraint_effect\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Presentation-level contribution。Median reviewer 可能 suggest 改进但不会 因为 visualization 加分或扣分。\\n\\n\\n可视化是 presentation quality 问题而非科学证据。Median reviewer 会在 minor comments 中评价：\\\"Figure X clearly shows the L0 dominance pattern\\\"  或 \\\"the compounding curve would benefit from error bars.\\\" 不影响 score 但 好的可视化可以帮助 reviewer 快速理解 compounding 现象。关键是 heatmap 要 展示 Qwen（spread, L0 cluster 明显）vs Yi（spike, 单个 L4H3 突出）vs  Gemma-2（flat, 无显著差异）的对比——如果只展示 Qwen，reviewer 会说  \\\"cherry-picked visualization.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"K/V Separation\",\n    \"description\": \"K 和 V heads 作为独立 MCKP items，独立 budget allocation。与 joint K=V 方法对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"kv_sep_ppl\": 11.22,\n      \"joint_kv_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"delta_sep_vs_joint\": 0.31,\n      \"sep_k_2bit_count\": 16,\n      \"sep_v_uniform_4bit\": true,\n      \"kv_asymmetric_heads\": 21\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: K/V Separation vs Joint (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Joint K=V (k=8)\",\n            \"ppl\": 10.91,\n            \"k_2bit\": 8,\n            \"v_2bit\": 0\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"K/V Separation\",\n            \"ppl\": 11.22,\n            \"k_2bit\": 16,\n            \"v_2bit\": 0\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            \"ppl\": 15.45,\n            \"k_2bit\": 0,\n            \"v_2bit\": 0\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Negative result 但 informative。在 median 档中被视为 thorough ablation， 可放 appendix。不影响核心 claim。\\n\\n\\nK/V separation 反而 worse（11.22 vs 10.91, +0.31 PPL）。separation 给 K heads  分配了 16 个 2-bit（超过 max_2bit=8 的 joint 约束），导致 K cache compounding。 V heads 在 separation 下全部 4-bit（optimal for V），但 K cache 的退化超过了 V 的收益。Median reviewer 会认为这是 negative result 但有 insight value： \\\"K cache is more sensitive to 2-bit compounding than V — this explains why  joint K=V treatment with a single cardinality constraint works better.\\\"  一位 reviewer 可能 suggest \\\"apply per-cache-type cardinality constraint\\\"  as future work。不会成为 major objection。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Downstream Task Evaluation (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n    \"description\": \"ARC-C / HellaSwag / PIQA / WinoGrande 在 Qwen2.5-7B 4× 压缩下评估。 验证 PPL improvement 转化为 downstream performance。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"arc_c_uniform\": 0.4812,\n      \"arc_c_mckp\": 0.5137,\n      \"arc_c_delta_pp\": 3.16,\n      \"hellaswag_uniform\": 0.7284,\n      \"hellaswag_mckp\": 0.7684,\n      \"hellaswag_delta_pp\": 4.0,\n      \"piqa_uniform\": 0.7661,\n      \"piqa_mckp\": 0.7786,\n      \"piqa_delta_pp\": 1.25,\n      \"winogrande_uniform\": 0.6622,\n      \"winogrande_mckp\": 0.6819,\n      \"winogrande_delta_pp\": 1.97,\n      \"avg_recovery\": 0.728,\n      \"bf16_avg\": 0.688\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Downstream Evaluation — Full Cross-Architecture\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen (Spread)\",\n            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"+2.60\",\n            \"arc_c_delta\": \"+3.16\",\n            \"verdict\": \"Benefit\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Yi-1.5 (Spike)\",\n            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"-0.77\",\n            \"arc_c_delta\": \"-3.24\",\n            \"verdict\": \"Degradation\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Llama (Spike)\",\n            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"-0.99\",\n            \"arc_c_delta\": \"-2.65\",\n            \"verdict\": \"Degradation\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Mistral (Flat)\",\n            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"-0.48\",\n            \"arc_c_delta\": \"-1.19\",\n            \"verdict\": \"Degradation\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Gemma-2 (Flat)\",\n            \"avg_delta_pp\": \"+0.14\",\n            \"arc_c_delta\": \"-0.17\",\n            \"verdict\": \"Noise\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中这是 double-edged evidence。Qwen 的 downstream gains 被认可但 限定为 \\\"architecture-specific\\\"。跨架构 degradation 要求论文措辞从 \\\"non-uniform improves downstream\\\" 改为 \\\"non-uniform allocation improves downstream  performance specifically on architectures with spread sensitivity patterns (1/5  tested); on other architectures, uniform 4-bit should be preferred.\\\"  arc_challenge 系统性退化需要主动讨论段落。\\n\\n\\nQwen downstream gains 一致 positive（+1.25 to +4.00pp），与 PPL improvement  方向一致。但 median reviewer 的核心 objection 是 A4：\\\"this only works on Qwen.\\\" 跨架构 downstream 数据显示 Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp,  Gemma-2 +0.14pp（noise）。reviewer 会写：\\\"4/5 architectures show negative or  negligible downstream effect. The method degrades downstream performance on most  models.\\\" 另一个 median-specific concern 是 lack of multi-seed CI：3.16pp arc_c  delta 没有 confidence interval，\\\"could be within single-run variance\\\"（A6）。 已有 qwen_3seed_downstream_ci（arc_c std=0.0035, hellaswag std=0.0022） 可部分回应。arc_challenge 跨模型系统性退化（Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp,  Mistral -1.19pp）会被特别标注——reviewer 要求主动讨论这个 pattern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"70B Profiling-Only\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-72B 上做 distortion profiling（不做 full eval），分析 sensitivity  patterns 是否随模型大小 scale。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"killed\",\n      \"sensitivity_pattern_observed\": null,\n      \"l0_dominance_scales\": null\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Missing data。Median reviewer 标注为 limitation，不作为 reject reason。\\n\\n\\n实验被 killed（可能 OOM 或 timeout）。Median reviewer 会注意到 \\\"only 7B-14B  scale models tested\\\" 并标注为 limitation：\\\"no evidence that findings generalize  to production-scale models (70B+).\\\" 但在 median 档中这是 minor gap 而非 major  objection——大多数 KV cache quantization papers 也只测 7B-14B。缺少 70B 数据 会降低 \\\"practical implications\\\" 的说服力但不会导致 reject。建议在 limitations  中明确承认 \\\"our experiments are limited to 7B-14B scale; scaling behavior of  compounding effects to 70B+ models remains an open question.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"L0-Only Heuristic Baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"最简单的 non-uniform 策略：L0 heads 8-bit，其余 uniform 4-bit。如果 L0-only 匹配 MCKP，full optimization 不必要。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"qwen_l0_random_mean\": 11.69,\n      \"qwen_l0_random_std\": 0.47,\n      \"qwen_l0_random_median\": 11.52,\n      \"qwen_naive_positional_ppl\": 12.23,\n      \"llama_mckp_ppl\": 8.45,\n      \"llama_l0_random_mean\": 10.48,\n      \"llama_naive_positional\": 9.94,\n      \"mistral_mckp_ppl\": 7.16,\n      \"mistral_l0_random_mean\": 7.56,\n      \"mistral_naive_positional\": 7.48,\n      \"mckp_consistently_beats_l0_random\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: MCKP vs Heuristic Baselines (budget=0.25)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen\",\n            \"mckp\": 10.91,\n            \"l0_random_median\": 11.52,\n            \"naive_positional\": 12.23,\n            \"uniform\": 15.45\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Llama\",\n            \"mckp\": 8.45,\n            \"l0_random_median\": 10.04,\n            \"naive_positional\": 9.94,\n            \"uniform\": 8.47\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Mistral\",\n            \"mckp\": 7.16,\n            \"l0_random_median\": 7.59,\n            \"naive_positional\": 7.48,\n            \"uniform\": 7.13\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median reviewer 认为这是 critical missing baseline 被补充后的 adequate response。 MCKP vs L0-random gap（5-16%）证明 solver 在 constraint-respecting 方案中仍有 optimization 价值。但 Mistral 的 MCKP(7.16) > uniform(7.13) 再次说明 flat  architecture 上任何 non-uniform 都是 net negative。\\n\\n\\nL0-only heuristic 的 PPL（Qwen median 11.52, mean 11.69）consistently worse  than MCKP（10.91），差距 -5.2%。这说明 profiling-based allocation 在 constraint  内仍有 optimization value——不仅仅是 \\\"protect L0 and done.\\\" Median reviewer  反应正面但有 nuance：(a) \\\"MCKP beats L0-random by 5.2% — meaningful but not  dramatic. The naive positional heuristic (12.23) is much worse, so profiling does  matter.\\\" (b) \\\"seed variance in L0-random is large (std=0.47, range 11.33-12.52),  suggesting the specific choice of which non-L0 heads get 2-bit matters significantly.\\\"  (c) Llama 和 Mistral 上 MCKP vs L0-random gap 更大（Llama: 8.45 vs 10.04 median,  -15.8%），说明 even on non-benefit architectures, random constraint-respecting  allocation is much worse than MCKP — the solver finds better allocations even when  the absolute PPL difference vs uniform is small. 这个 experiment 的原始设计被 kill 但后来用 corrected version (l0_heuristic_corrected) 完成。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Greedy + Cardinality Constraint Ablation (Solver Equivalence)\",\n    \"description\": \"RateQuant greedy + max_2bit=k 约束。对比 (a) greedy unconstrained,  (b) greedy constrained k=8, (c) MCKP constrained k=8。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n      \"greedy_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"delta_greedy_vs_mckp_constrained\": 0.0012,\n      \"bit_distribution_identical\": true,\n      \"distribution\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Solver Equivalence Under Constraint (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"solver\": \"Greedy unconstrained\",\n            \"ppl\": 32.45,\n            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\",\n            \"status\": \"FAIL\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"solver\": \"Greedy + max_2bit=8\",\n            \"ppl\": 11.23,\n            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\",\n            \"status\": \"PASS\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"solver\": \"MCKP + max_2bit=8\",\n            \"ppl\": 11.23,\n            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\",\n            \"status\": \"PASS\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"solver\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            \"ppl\": 15.45,\n            \"bit_dist\": \"all 4-bit\",\n            \"status\": \"baseline\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中被认可为 paper 的 highlight。两位 reviewer 会引用此结果支持 \\\"the constraint is the contribution\\\" narrative。但第三位 reviewer 用此结果 反驳 \\\"then what exactly is the technical contribution — discovering that you need  a max_2bit cap? That's a hyperparameter, not a method.\\\"\\n\\n\\n这是 paper 最 powerful 的单个实验：constrained greedy = constrained MCKP  (Δ=0.0012 PPL, identical bit distribution)。证明 constraint 是唯一 intervention  that matters——两个算法复杂度完全不同的 solver 在 constraint 下产生相同解。 Median reviewer 对此实验的反应最 positive：\\\"this is the strongest evidence in the  paper — it shows the cardinality constraint is the real contribution, not the  optimization algorithm.\\\" 但也引发 A3 concern：\\\"if a simple cardinality constraint  is all you need, this is essentially one hyperparameter — is that a sufficient  contribution for a main conference paper?\\\" Reviewer 会要求 (a) 更强的 principled  justification for why cardinality constraint works（不只是 empirical observation）， (b) 讨论 constraint 与 RateQuant 的 distortion model 的关系。Qwen14b 上也验证了 solver equivalence（greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0），增加了 generality。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Error Bars\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B 上 3 个不同 calibration seed 的 constrained MCKP，报告 mean±std。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mckp_seed0\": 11.02,\n      \"mckp_seed1\": 10.9,\n      \"mckp_seed2\": 11.05,\n      \"mckp_mean\": 10.99,\n      \"mckp_std\": 0.065,\n      \"bit_dist_all_seeds\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\",\n      \"allocation_agreement_3way\": 0.902,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"improvement_significant\": true,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 11.12,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 10.86\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Multi-Seed PPL Stability (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"seed\": 0,\n            \"ppl\": 11.02,\n            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"seed\": 1,\n            \"ppl\": 10.9,\n            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"seed\": 2,\n            \"ppl\": 11.05,\n            \"bit_dist\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"seed\": \"mean±std\",\n            \"ppl\": \"10.99±0.065\",\n            \"bit_dist\": \"consistent\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median reviewer 接受 PPL 层面的 statistical credibility 但要求 downstream CI。 这是 median 档的 typical gap——不至于 reject 但会是 \\\"requested revision\\\" 的一部分。\\n\\n\\nstd=0.065 意味着 95% CI 约 [10.86, 11.12]，远低于 uniform 15.45——improvement  统计上 robust。Bit distribution 在所有 seed 下一致（{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}）， allocation agreement 90.2% 跨 seed。Median reviewer 会认可 PPL stability 但有 两个 residual concerns：(a) \\\"3 seeds is the minimum — 5 seeds with proper CI would  be more convincing\\\"（minor revision level），(b) \\\"allocation agreement 90.2% means  10% of heads flip between seeds — which heads and how does it affect downstream?\\\"  更严重的是 A6：**缺少 multi-seed downstream CI**。PPL multi-seed 已有，但  downstream 的 arc_c +3.16pp 没有 error bar。qwen_3seed_downstream_ci 提供了 部分数据（arc_c std=0.0035），但只在 Qwen 上。Reviewer 会标注 \\\"multi-seed  downstream CI missing for non-Qwen architectures\\\" 作为 significant gap。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Runtime/Latency Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"End-to-end inference latency 和 throughput，mixed-precision KV cache vs uniform 4-bit。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bf16_prefill_ms\": 45.86,\n      \"bf16_decode_ms\": 33.78,\n      \"bf16_throughput\": 29.6,\n      \"uniform4_prefill_ms\": 54.25,\n      \"uniform4_decode_ms\": 42.46,\n      \"uniform4_throughput\": 23.6,\n      \"mckp_prefill_ms\": 57.03,\n      \"mckp_decode_ms\": 46.09,\n      \"mckp_throughput\": 21.8,\n      \"mckp_solver_time_sec\": 0.005,\n      \"memory_compression_4x\": true,\n      \"mckp_overhead_vs_uniform_pct\": 8.5,\n      \"mckp_overhead_vs_bf16_pct\": 36.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table: Runtime Benchmark (Qwen2.5-7B, seq_len=2048)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"BF16 (no quantization)\",\n            \"prefill_ms\": 45.86,\n            \"decode_ms\": 33.78,\n            \"throughput\": 29.6,\n            \"memory_MB\": 21\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            \"prefill_ms\": 54.25,\n            \"decode_ms\": 42.46,\n            \"throughput\": 23.6,\n            \"memory_MB\": 5.25\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Constrained MCKP\",\n            \"prefill_ms\": 57.03,\n            \"decode_ms\": 46.09,\n            \"throughput\": 21.8,\n            \"memory_MB\": 5.25\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档中这是 second major objection source。Runtime overhead 与  \\\"practical implications\\\" claim 冲突。Paper 需要 reframe：\\\"memory-bound  scenarios (long context, large batch) where 4× memory reduction enables  deployment that bf16 cannot.\\\" 8K context 实验（qwen7b_8k_context_eval:  uniform 77.75 vs MCKP 8.59）是 strongest counterargument——at long context,  memory savings dominate and quality gap amplifies dramatically。\\n\\n令人意外的 negative finding：mixed-precision MCKP 比 uniform 4-bit 更慢 （throughput 21.8 vs 23.6 tok/s, -7.6%），甚至比 bf16 baseline 更慢 （21.8 vs 29.6 tok/s, -26.4%）。原因是 mixed-precision 需要 per-head 不同 的 dequantization kernel，当前实现缺少 fused kernel optimization。 Median reviewer 反应强烈 negative：\\\"the method provides 29% PPL improvement  on Qwen but costs 8% throughput — practitioners would need to decide if PPL  improvement justifies speed regression. On 7/8 architectures where there's no  PPL benefit, the speed cost is pure overhead.\\\" 这成为 major objection 之一（A6  范畴）。MCKP solver 本身只需 0.005s（negligible），所以 overhead 完全来自 inference-time mixed-precision dequantization。需要在 paper 中承认 \\\"current  implementation uses naive per-head dequantization; a fused kernel could eliminate  the overhead\\\" 并标注为 engineering limitation, not fundamental。但 reviewer 会 counter：\\\"without the optimized kernel, the practical benefit claim is weakened.\\\"\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":725,"startLine":1,"totalLines":725}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HLq16YamsYpowTZ5FjasR3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — ratekv\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\n5\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (11 days from today 2026-05-14)\n6\t- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n7\t\n8\t## bf16 Consistency Resolution (2026-05-14)\n9\t\n10\t**已解决**：qwen_bf16_reeval 确认 bf16 ≈ fp16（baseline delta=0.0006, uniform delta=0.005）。compounding_sweep bf16 rerun 不需要。\n11\t\n12\t**eval pipeline 一致性**：exp_e 使用了不同的 eval 参数（baseline=8.82, MCKP=9.57），与主 pipeline（baseline=9.81）不一致。hires_mckp_reeval 用统一 pipeline 重测：MCKP hires bf16=10.9131。**论文使用统一 pipeline 数字**。\n13\t\n14\t| 指标 | 统一 pipeline (bf16) | exp_e pipeline (bf16) | fp16 (旧) |\n15\t|------|---------------------|----------------------|-----------|\n16\t| Baseline | **9.8106** | 8.819 | 9.81 |\n17\t| Uniform 4-bit | **15.4454** | — | 15.45 |\n18\t| MCKP hires (max_2bit=8) | **10.9131** | 9.569 | — |\n19\t| MCKP lowres (max_2bit=8) | ~11.23 | 11.345 | 11.23 |\n20\t\n21\t## Core Insight\n22\t\n23\tPer-head KV cache quantization on hardware-aligned bit-widths {2,4,8,16} has an unreported universal failure mode: 2-bit quantization distortions compound non-additively through the residual stream, causing ALL tested unconstrained solvers (greedy, MCKP) to systematically over-allocate 2-bit heads and underperform uniform 4-bit across 8/8 architectures (1.07×–3.31× baseline). A cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) universally prevents this over-allocation, and furthermore reduces the feasible set to where solver choice becomes irrelevant (greedy = MCKP, Δ=0.0000). Under moderate compression (4×), only 1/8 architectures benefits from non-uniform allocation over uniform 4-bit — providing the first empirical evidence that the implicit assumption \"non-uniform is always better than uniform\" is wrong in KV cache quantization. The core contribution is the compounding effect discovery + universal constraint fix, not the allocation algorithm.\n24\t\n25\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n26\t\n27\t1. **2-bit compounding is a universal failure mode for unconstrained per-head allocation**: On hardware-aligned non-consecutive bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, per-head independent profiling distortions compound non-additively when multiple heads are simultaneously assigned 2-bit quantization. This causes ALL tested unconstrained solvers to over-allocate 2-bit heads and underperform uniform 4-bit across 8/8 diverse architectures (Qwen 3.31×, Gemma-2 1.47×, Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×, Pythia, Qwen-14B, Phi-3-medium). Quantitative evidence of non-additivity: per-head profiling predicts joint PPL ≈11 but actual joint 2-bit PPL is 32–37 (3× prediction error). This is the first systematic characterization of compounding effects in per-head KV cache quantization. Long-context amplifies the failure: at 8K tokens, uniform 4-bit degrades 11.15× baseline while constrained MCKP degrades only 1.23× — a 9× gap in degradation rate.\n28\t\n29\t2. **A cardinality constraint is the universal fix — and makes solver choice irrelevant**: A simple cardinality constraint (max_2bit ≤ k) is sufficient to prevent compounding across ALL tested architectures. Three universally beneficial properties: (a) prevents catastrophic over-allocation on sensitive architectures (Qwen: 32.45 → 10.91), (b) prevents moderate over-allocation on flat architectures (Gemma-2: 8.85 → 6.17, reducing 2-bit heads from 106 to 8), (c) reduces the feasible set to where solver choice is irrelevant — constrained greedy and constrained MCKP produce IDENTICAL bit allocations and PPL (Δ=0.0000). The constraint is parameterizable via small-scale compounding test (k≤8 universally safe: <2.5% degradation across all architectures). Practical implication: practitioners need only add one integer parameter to existing pipelines.\n30\t\n31\t3. **Non-uniform allocation benefit is rare — most models should use uniform 4-bit**: Under moderate compression (4×), only 1/8 tested architectures (Qwen2.5-7B, \"spread\" sensitivity pattern) benefits from non-uniform allocation (+27.3% PPL, +1.9pp downstream avg). The remaining 7/8 show no benefit or minor degradation (<1pp avg downstream). A 2-metric empirical diagnostic (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70) correctly classifies all 9 tested models (9/9 accuracy), providing practitioners a simple check: if the diagnostic says \"no\" — skip profiling and use uniform 4-bit with zero quality loss. This is the first systematic study of *when* non-uniform KV cache quantization is beneficial, correcting the implicit assumption that it always helps.\n32\t\n33\t## Story Spine\n34\t\n35\t- **Problem**: Per-head mixed-precision KV cache quantization promises better quality-compression tradeoffs than uniform bit-width. But on hardware-aligned non-consecutive bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, we discover that existing allocation algorithms (greedy, MCKP) systematically FAIL — producing worse results than naive uniform 4-bit across ALL tested architectures. The failure mode is unreported: 2-bit quantization distortions compound non-additively, and solvers consistently over-allocate 2-bit heads. Meanwhile, the field implicitly assumes non-uniform allocation always helps, but no systematic study has tested this across architectures.\n36\t\n37\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: RateQuant provides R-D optimal per-head allocation via continuous closed-form and discrete greedy (optimal on consecutive integers {2,...,6}). KIVI and ARKV apply uniform or heuristic mixed-precision. However, on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}: (a) RateQuant's greedy produces PPL 32.45 vs optimal ~10.91 — polymatroid optimality breaks, (b) unconstrained MCKP fares even worse (PPL 36.92) due to compounding, (c) NO prior work addresses *when* non-uniform allocation is actually beneficial vs when uniform suffices.\n38\t\n39\t- **Our framing**: We present three contributions: (1) the first characterization of 2-bit compounding effects in per-head KV cache quantization — showing that profiling non-additivity causes ALL unconstrained solvers to fail on {2,4,8,16} across 8/8 architectures; (2) a simple universal fix: a cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) that prevents compounding, makes solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000), and is safely parameterizable (k≤8 universally safe); (3) the first systematic study of *when* non-uniform allocation helps — answer: rarely (1/8 architectures at moderate compression), with a 2-metric diagnostic (9/9 correct) that tells practitioners whether to invest in profiling or just use uniform 4-bit.\n40\t\n41\t- **Headline result template**: \"We show that per-head KV cache quantization on hardware-aligned bit-widths has a universal failure mode: 2-bit distortions compound non-additively, causing ALL unconstrained solvers to underperform uniform 4-bit across 8 architectures. A cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) universally fixes this, making solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000). Surprisingly, under moderate compression, only 1/8 architectures benefits from non-uniform allocation at all — most models should simply use uniform 4-bit. A 2-metric diagnostic (9/9 accuracy) provides practitioners a simple check to determine when profiling is worthwhile. At long context (8K tokens), the constraint reduces degradation from 11.15× to 1.23× baseline, demonstrating critical deployment value.\"\n42\t\n43\t## \"When Does Non-Uniform Allocation Help?\" — Analysis Chapter\n44\t\n45\tFive case studies representing the full spectrum of heterogeneity:\n46\t\n47\t| Case | Model | GQA | Top-5% Conc. | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Role in Paper |\n48\t|------|-------|-----|--------------|------------------------------|---------------|\n49\t| **Strong positive** | Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 0.59-0.66 | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Primary showcase; \"spread\" pattern (L0 cluster, 4 heads, 26× dominance) |\n50\t| **GQA counterexample** | Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 0.71 (hires) | ≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22) | Highest GQA but no benefit; \"spike\" pattern (L4H3 single outlier, 64% of total delta) |\n51\t| **Marginal** | Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 0.57 (hires) | +0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47) | Boundary condition; constraint never binds (natural k=2) |\n52\t| **Negative** | Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 0.22 (hires) | -0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13) | Profiler zero-signal; monotonic k-PPL curve |\n53\t| **Strongest negative** | Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 0.23 (hires) | -0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03) | Low-end anchor; most uniform sensitivity (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) |\n54\t\n55\t**Spike vs Spread insight**: Yi-1.5 vs Qwen illustrates why GQA ratio alone is insufficient. Both have high GQA (8:1 vs 7:1), but Qwen's L0 *cluster* of sensitive heads creates optimization opportunities for MCKP, while Yi-1.5's single extreme outlier (L4H3) cannot be exploited — the solver assigns 8-bit to that one head but has no other heads to differentiate. Distribution shape matters more than the existence of outliers.\n56\t\n57\t**Compression amplifies benefit**: Even on low-heterogeneity Llama, aggressive 5.3× compression yields constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 (45× better).\n58\t\n59\t**Joint diagnostic** (n=8, 8/8 correct): concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 → non-uniform allocation recommended (spread pattern). Either condition violated → uniform suffices at moderate compression; non-uniform still valuable at aggressive compression. Yi-1.5 (concentration 0.71 but t₁/t₅=0.90 — spike), CodeLlama (0.80, t₁/t₅=0.81 — spike), and Qwen (0.61, t₁/t₅=0.57 — spread) illustrate why concentration alone is insufficient.\n60\t\n61\t## Solver Equivalence Evidence (plan_016, CONFIRMED ✅)\n62\t\n63\t| Method | PPL | Bit Distribution | Budget |\n64\t|--------|-----|-------------------|--------|\n65\t| Greedy unconstrained | 32.45 | {2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10} | 0.25 |\n66\t| MCKP unconstrained | 36.92 | — | 0.25 |\n67\t| **Greedy + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n68\t| **MCKP + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n69\t| Uniform 4-bit | 15.4454 | all 4-bit | 0.25 |\n70\t\n71\tKey takeaway: The constraint is the primary intervention — without it, both solvers fail; with it, solver choice is irrelevant (Δ=0.0000). This powerfully demonstrates the constraint is THE contribution.\n72\t\n73\t## Cross-Architecture Evidence Summary\n74\t\n75\t| Model | GQA | KV Heads | Top-5% Conc. | Unconstrained ×baseline (W2 v2) | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Distribution Shape | Conclusion |\n76\t|-------|-----|----------|--------------|--------------------------------|------------------------------|-------------------|------------|\n77\t| Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 112 | **0.61** | **3.31× (32.45)** ☠️ | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Spread (L0 cluster, 4 heads) | ✅ Strong benefit |\n78\t| Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 192 | **0.71** (hires) | 1.08× (7.56) | **≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22)** | Spike (L4H3 single outlier) | ❌ GQA counterexample |\n79\t| Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 256 | **0.57** (hires) | 1.07× (8.63) | **+0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47)** | Spike (t₁/t₅≈0.85, single dominant L2H5) | ≈ Marginal |\n80\t| Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 256 | **0.22** (hires) | 1.08× (7.57) | **-0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13)** | Flat (profiler zero-signal) | ❌ Negative |\n81\t| Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 336 | **0.23** (hires) | 1.47× (8.85) | **-0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03)** | Flat (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) | ❌ Strongest negative |\n82\t\n83\t**Unconstrained pattern** (W2 v2, all WikiText-2 test eval, gradient narrative): Unconstrained degradation follows a **concentration-dependent gradient**, not a binary catastrophe/benign split:\n84\t- **Spread** (Qwen, conc=0.61): **3.31×** catastrophic — L0 cluster creates massive compounding\n85\t- **Flat-high-2bit** (Gemma-2, conc=0.23): **1.47×** moderate — solver assigns 106/336=31.5% heads to 2-bit because distortions are indistinguishable (CV=1.28), cumulative effect significant despite small per-head delta\n86\t- **Spike/Flat-low-2bit** (Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×): mild — solver selects few 2-bit heads (Yi 11.5%, Llama 4.7%, Mistral 16.4%)\n87\t- In ALL cases unconstrained ≤ uniform 4-bit — solver consistently over-allocates 2-bit heads\n88\t\n89\t**Gemma-2 1.47× must be discussed in paper** (Reviewer mandate, severity: warning):\n90\t\n91\tThree-tier labeling (NOT binary catastrophe/benign):\n92\t- **Catastrophic** (3.31×): Spread model (Qwen) — L0 cluster compounding\n93\t- **Moderate** (1.47×): Flat-high-2bit (Gemma-2) — solver over-allocation from indistinguishable distortions\n94\t- **Mild** (1.07-1.08×): Spike/Flat-low-2bit (Yi, Llama, Mistral)\n95\t\n96\tReviewer-suggested paragraph for paper (1 段, 3-4 句):\n97\t\"Gemma-2-9B exhibits a moderate 1.47× degradation under unconstrained allocation, higher than the 1.07–1.08× observed in other non-Spread models. This stems from its flat sensitivity distribution (concentration 0.23, CV 1.28): the solver cannot meaningfully differentiate heads, leading to 31.5% of heads assigned to 2-bit (vs 4.7–16.4% in other models). While not catastrophic, this over-allocation still motivates the cardinality constraint even on flat-distribution architectures. The constraint reduces 2-bit heads from 106 to 8, yielding PPL within 0.3% of uniform — confirming that the constraint universally prevents solver over-allocation regardless of distribution shape.\"\n98\t\n99\tThis **strengthens** the paper: (1) honesty → credibility, (2) constraint has universal value (not just Spread), (3) explains solver degradation mechanism under low signal → added insight depth.\n100\t\n101\t⚠️ **Data file note**: `artifacts/w2_unconstrained_v2_results.json` still has old Gemma-2 BOS bug data (baseline=711.6). Fix in `artifacts/w2_gemma2_bos_fix_results.json`. Agent tasked to merge.\n102\t\n103\t**Key pattern**: Constrained allocation benefit depends on the joint condition (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70, 5/5 correct), NOT GQA ratio or concentration alone. Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, concentration 0.71 — highest — yet no benefit) vs Qwen (GQA 7:1, concentration 0.61, +27.3%) demonstrates that neither GQA nor concentration alone is a reliable proxy. The critical factor is sensitivity *distribution shape*: spread (multiple heads with cross-bitwidth gradients) enables MCKP, while spike (single outlier) or flat (uniform sensitivity) does not.\n104\t\n105\t**Aggressive compression** (Llama): At 5.3× compression, constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 — prevents catastrophic collapse even on low-heterogeneity architectures.\n106\t\n107\t### Mistral k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n108\t\n109\tPPL monotonically increases with k — every additional 2-bit head hurts. Even best k=4 (PPL 7.1648) is worse than uniform (7.131).\n110\t\n111\t| k | PPL | 2-bit | 4-bit | 8-bit | 16-bit | mem |\n112\t|---|-----|-------|-------|-------|--------|-----|\n113\t| 4 | **7.1648** | 4 | 252 | 0 | 0 | 0.248 |\n114\t| 8 | 7.1997 | 8 | 247 | 0 | 1 | 0.249 |\n115\t| 12 | 7.2448 | 12 | 242 | 0 | 2 | 0.250 |\n116\t| 16 | 7.3106 | 16 | 238 | 0 | 2 | 0.248 |\n117\t| 18 | 7.3231 | 18 | 235 | 0 | 3 | 0.250 |\n118\t| uniform 4-bit | 7.131 | 0 | 256 | 0 | 0 | 0.250 |\n119\t\n120\tContrast with Qwen (U-shaped, optimal k=8) and Llama (flat, natural k=2). Mistral's monotonic pattern confirms profiler zero-signal: no head benefits from 2-bit downgrade.\n121\t\n122\t### Llama k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n123\t\n124\tAll k values produce identical PPL=8.4498. MCKP naturally selects only 2 heads for 2-bit — constraint never binds. Marginal +0.2% over uniform (8.4498 vs 8.469).\n125\t\n126\t### Downstream Eval — Cross-Architecture (W3, 0-shot, 5 tasks)\n127\t\n128\t**Qwen2.5-7B (Spread) — MCKP benefits translate to downstream** ✅\n129\t\n130\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP hires | Δ | BF16 Baseline |\n131\t|------|---------------|------------|---|---------------|\n132\t| ARC-C | 0.4812 | 0.5137 | **+3.16pp** | 0.5290 |\n133\t| HellaSwag | 0.7284 | 0.7684 | **+4.00pp** | 0.7833 |\n134\t| PIQA | 0.7661 | 0.7786 | **+1.25pp** | 0.7932 |\n135\t| WinoGrande | 0.6622 | 0.6819 | **+1.97pp** | 0.6898 |\n136\t| **Avg recovery** | — | — | **72.8%** | — |\n137\t\n138\t**Yi-1.5-9B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n139\t\n140\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n141\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n142\t| arc_easy | 0.7946 | 0.7854 | -0.92pp |\n143\t| arc_challenge | 0.5205 | 0.4881 | **-3.24pp** |\n144\t| hellaswag | 0.5857 | 0.5797 | -0.60pp |\n145\t| piqa | 0.7927 | 0.7894 | -0.33pp |\n146\t| winogrande | 0.7174 | 0.7301 | +1.27pp |\n147\t| **Average** | **0.6822** | **0.6745** | **-0.77pp** |\n148\t\n149\t**Llama-3.1-8B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n150\t\n151\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n152\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n153\t| arc_easy | 0.8173 | 0.8039 | -1.34pp |\n154\t| arc_challenge | 0.5256 | 0.4991 | **-2.65pp** |\n155\t| hellaswag | 0.6026 | 0.6012 | -0.14pp |\n156\t| piqa | 0.7867 | 0.7802 | -0.65pp |\n157\t| winogrande | 0.7253 | 0.7238 | -0.15pp |\n158\t| **Average** | **0.6915** | **0.6816** | **-0.99pp** |\n159\t\n160\t**Mistral-7B-v0.3 (Flat) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n161\t\n162\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=4) | Δ |\n163\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n164\t| arc_easy | — | — | — |\n165\t| arc_challenge | — | — | — |\n166\t| hellaswag | — | — | — |\n167\t| piqa | — | — | — |\n168\t| winogrande | — | — | — |\n169\t| **Average** | **0.6894** | **0.6846** | **-0.48pp** |\n170\t\n171\t**Gemma-2-9B (Flat) — Negligible MCKP effect, noise range** (W3)\n172\t\n173\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | Δ |\n174\t|------|---------------|------|---|\n175\t| **Average** | **0.7251** | **0.7265** | **+0.14pp** (noise) |\n176\t\n177\t**Downstream summary (Reviewer-verified framing)**:\n178\t- Diagnostic correctly predicts both PPL and downstream outcomes across **all 5 tested models**\n179\t- Spread (Qwen): consistent downstream gains (+1.25 to +4.00pp)\n180\t- Non-Spread (4 models): MCKP shows **minor systematic degradation** vs uniform (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp noise)\n181\t- **Llama signal**: 0/5 tasks where MCKP ≥ uniform — degradation is systematic, not task-specific noise\n182\t- arc_challenge shows largest per-task effect (Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp)\n183\t- **Paper must**: (a) report full per-task tables, not just averages, (b) use \"shows minor degradation\" NOT \"preserves accuracy\" — the latter has spin, (c) note arc_challenge as worst-case explicitly\n184\t- **Limitation**: no multi-seed CI for downstream — 0-shot arc_challenge -3.24pp could be questioned for significance\n185\t- **arc_challenge 系统性信号** (Reviewer 观察): arc_challenge 退化跨模型一致（Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp, Mistral -1.19pp, Gemma-2 -0.17pp），不是随机噪声。论文应主动讨论：\"ARC-Challenge shows the largest per-task sensitivity to allocation strategy, consistent with its reliance on multi-step reasoning where subtle KV cache errors accumulate.\"\n186\t- **呈现方式**: 主表放完整 per-task 数据，文字用均值+range 概括。建议措辞：\"Across four non-Spread architectures, constrained MCKP shows minor average degradation vs uniform 4-bit (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp). Per-task variation ranges from +1.27pp (Yi, WinoGrande) to -3.24pp (Yi, ARC-Challenge).\"\n187\t\n188\t## Allocation Baseline Evidence (plan_015, mckp_reeval)\n189\t\n190\tAll numbers from unified bf16 eval pipeline, budget=0.25.\n191\t\n192\t| Model | Baseline | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | L0-random (mean±std) | L0-random (median) | Naive Positional | MCKP improvement |\n193\t|-------|----------|---------------|------|----------------------|---------------------|------------------|------------------|\n194\t| Qwen2.5-7B (k=8) | 9.8106 | 15.4454 | 10.9131 | 11.691±0.422 | **11.515** | 12.230 | 27.3% vs uniform (standard); 29.4% (hires, §5.4) |\n195\t| Llama-3.1-8B (k=2) | 8.0918 | 8.469 | 8.4498 | 10.479±1.033 | **10.038** | 9.941 | +0.2% vs uniform |\n196\t| Mistral-7B-v0.3 (k=4) | 7.035 | 7.131 | 7.1648 | 7.560±0.087 | **7.586** | 7.481 | -0.4% vs uniform |\n197\t\n198\t**Outlier note**: seed_4 inflates mean on Qwen (12.51) and Llama (12.44). Median is more robust: Qwen median 11.515 vs mean 11.691 (−0.176); Llama median 10.038 vs mean 10.479 (−0.441). Mistral has no outlier (median ≈ mean). Paper should report both mean±std and median.\n199\t\n200\t**MCKP vs L0-random (median)**: Qwen 10.91 vs 11.52 (−5.2%); Llama 8.45 vs 10.04 (−15.8%); Mistral 7.16 vs 7.59 (−5.7%). MCKP consistently outperforms random L0-constrained allocation across all architectures.\n201\t\n202\t## Differentiation from RateQuant\n203\t\n204\t| Aspect | RateQuant | Ours |\n205\t|--------|-----------|------|\n206\t| Bit-width selection | Greedy on consecutive integers {2,...,6} (Prop. 6 optimal) + continuous closed-form (Thm. 2) | Cardinality-constrained allocation on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}-bit |\n207\t| Distortion model | Additive, parametric D(b)=α·β^{-b} | Additive + cardinality regularization for non-additivity |\n208\t| Compounding effects | Acknowledged (Appendix M) but unaddressed | **Core contribution**: cardinality constraint prevents compounding; first quantitative evidence |\n209\t| Action space | Consecutive integers (polymatroid → greedy optimal) | Non-consecutive hardware-aligned (polymatroid breaks → constraint needed, solver doesn't matter) |\n210\t| Solver requirement | Greedy (provably optimal in their setting) | **Any solver** — constrained greedy = constrained MCKP (Δ=0.0000 PPL) |\n211\t| K/V allocation | Asymmetric K/V budget (e.g. K=2.85, V=2.15) | MCKP/greedy treats K/V heads as independent items (natural extension) |\n212\t| **Applicability analysis** | **Not addressed — assumes non-uniform always helps** | **Systematic study of when non-uniform allocation is beneficial (new contribution)** |\n213\t\n214\t## Venue Fit Risks\n215\t\n216\t- **\"The constraint is just a heuristic, not a real contribution\"**: Strongest reviewer attack under new framing. Defense: (a) principled motivation from compounding effect non-additivity with first quantitative evidence, (b) constraint parameterization via systematic compounding test, (c) the finding that constraint alone makes solver choice irrelevant is a surprising and practically useful result — practitioners need only add one parameter to existing pipelines.\n217\t- **Incrementality over RateQuant**: Defense: (a) RateQuant's greedy is suboptimal unconstrained on {2,4,8,16} (PPL 32.45), (b) our constraint fixes RateQuant's greedy to match MCKP — we're improving their method, not replacing it, (c) applicability analysis is entirely new.\n218\t- **Method only strong on one architecture (Qwen)**: 5 models tested, only Qwen shows clear benefit. Mitigate: (a) analysis contribution framing — characterizing boundary conditions is more useful than universal positive, (b) honest negative/marginal results (Yi-1.5, Gemma-2, Mistral, Llama) strengthen credibility, (c) unlike prior work that assumes non-uniform always helps, we provide the first systematic study of *when it fails*, (d) Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, FAIL) is particularly powerful — it disproves the naive \"higher GQA = more benefit\" hypothesis and shows our diagnostic is needed.\n219\t- **GQA ratio is not a reliable proxy**: Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1) directly contradicts a GQA-based prediction. Do NOT present GQA ratio as a predictor — present it as one contributing factor. The reliable predictor is Top-5% concentration (0.50 threshold, 8/8 correct). The \"spike vs spread\" analysis explains WHY same-GQA models differ.\n220\t- **Statistical power**: n=8 models is directional evidence, not statistical claim. Do NOT claim \"significant correlation\" — use \"consistent pattern across 8 architectures\" or \"8/8 correctly classified by the 0.50 threshold.\"\n221\t- **No eviction arm**: Mention as negative finding; framework extends naturally to eviction.\n222\t\n223\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n224\t\n225\t1. **\"The cardinality constraint is trivial — just cap the extreme allocations\"** → (a) Trivial in retrospect, but without it both greedy (PPL 32.45) and MCKP (PPL 36.92) fail catastrophically — the failure mode is non-obvious, (b) principled motivation from compounding effect characterization (plan_004), (c) optimal k selection via systematic small-scale test, (d) the finding that this single intervention eliminates solver complexity is surprising and practically valuable.\n226\t2. **\"This is just RateQuant with a constraint added\"** → (a) We agree — and that's the point: RateQuant's greedy + our constraint achieves identical results to MCKP + constraint, (b) the constraint addresses a real gap: compounding effects on {2,4,8,16} that RateQuant acknowledges but doesn't solve, (c) applicability analysis is new.\n227\t3. **\"The method only works on Qwen — isn't this a Qwen paper?\"** → We systematically test 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1 and honestly report negative results (Gemma-2, Mistral). The analysis contribution — characterizing *boundary conditions* of non-uniform quantization — generalizes beyond any single model and is more useful than a universally positive but misleading claim.\n228\t4. **\"How does this work at different compression ratios?\"** → Budget sweep across 2×, 4×, 8× (plan_005). Aggressive compression on Llama shows benefit amplifies even on low-heterogeneity models.\n229\t5. **\"n=3/4/5 models is not enough for the heterogeneity claim\"** → Acknowledged as limitation. We present directional evidence across 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1, with a monotonic trend between GQA ratio, heterogeneity, and MCKP benefit. The Top-5% concentration diagnostic is a testable hypothesis, not a statistical claim.\n230\t6. **\"RateQuant does K/V asymmetric allocation, do you?\"** → Framework naturally treats K and V heads as independent items; plan_014 tests K/V separation.\n231\t7. **\"Where are the downstream task results?\"** → ✅ DONE (plan_012 + W3, all 5 models): Qwen (Spread): +1.25 to +4.00pp across 4 tasks, 72.8% avg recovery. Yi-1.5 (Spike): avg -0.77pp. Llama (Spike): avg -0.99pp (0/5 tasks positive — systematic). Mistral (Flat): avg -0.48pp. Gemma-2 (Flat): avg +0.14pp (noise). **Diagnostic predicts both PPL and downstream correctly across all 5 architectures**. Must report full per-task tables; use \"shows minor degradation\" not \"preserves accuracy\".\n232\t8. **\"The profiler distortion=0.0 on Mistral suggests the profiling method is broken\"** → Profiler correctly reports near-zero sensitivity differences. Some architectures genuinely have homogeneous head sensitivity, making non-uniform allocation futile.\n233\t9. **\"If solver doesn't matter, why present MCKP at all?\"** → (a) MCKP provides the formal framework for the constrained allocation problem — it's the lens through which we analyze the problem even if greedy solves it equally well, (b) presenting both solvers with identical results IS the evidence that the constraint is what matters, (c) for future extensions (more bit-widths, per-layer budgets), MCKP may regain advantage — we keep it as general framework.\n234\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc8fbc02-a351-42eb-9162-8abd7e156f3e","uuid":"20ef5691-ae61-422a-a839-9339559f1734","timestamp":"2026-05-16T02:37:22.370Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/ratekv/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T021448/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — ratekv\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (11 days from today 2026-05-14)\n- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n\n## bf16 Consistency Resolution (2026-05-14)\n\n**已解决**：qwen_bf16_reeval 确认 bf16 ≈ fp16（baseline delta=0.0006, uniform delta=0.005）。compounding_sweep bf16 rerun 不需要。\n\n**eval pipeline 一致性**：exp_e 使用了不同的 eval 参数（baseline=8.82, MCKP=9.57），与主 pipeline（baseline=9.81）不一致。hires_mckp_reeval 用统一 pipeline 重测：MCKP hires bf16=10.9131。**论文使用统一 pipeline 数字**。\n\n| 指标 | 统一 pipeline (bf16) | exp_e pipeline (bf16) | fp16 (旧) |\n|------|---------------------|----------------------|-----------|\n| Baseline | **9.8106** | 8.819 | 9.81 |\n| Uniform 4-bit | **15.4454** | — | 15.45 |\n| MCKP hires (max_2bit=8) | **10.9131** | 9.569 | — |\n| MCKP lowres (max_2bit=8) | ~11.23 | 11.345 | 11.23 |\n\n## Core Insight\n\nPer-head KV cache quantization on hardware-aligned bit-widths {2,4,8,16} has an unreported universal failure mode: 2-bit quantization distortions compound non-additively through the residual stream, causing ALL tested unconstrained solvers (greedy, MCKP) to systematically over-allocate 2-bit heads and underperform uniform 4-bit across 8/8 architectures (1.07×–3.31× baseline). A cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) universally prevents this over-allocation, and furthermore reduces the feasible set to where solver choice becomes irrelevant (greedy = MCKP, Δ=0.0000). Under moderate compression (4×), only 1/8 architectures benefits from non-uniform allocation over uniform 4-bit — providing the first empirical evidence that the implicit assumption \"non-uniform is always better than uniform\" is wrong in KV cache quantization. The core contribution is the compounding effect discovery + universal constraint fix, not the allocation algorithm.\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **2-bit compounding is a universal failure mode for unconstrained per-head allocation**: On hardware-aligned non-consecutive bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, per-head independent profiling distortions compound non-additively when multiple heads are simultaneously assigned 2-bit quantization. This causes ALL tested unconstrained solvers to over-allocate 2-bit heads and underperform uniform 4-bit across 8/8 diverse architectures (Qwen 3.31×, Gemma-2 1.47×, Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×, Pythia, Qwen-14B, Phi-3-medium). Quantitative evidence of non-additivity: per-head profiling predicts joint PPL ≈11 but actual joint 2-bit PPL is 32–37 (3× prediction error). This is the first systematic characterization of compounding effects in per-head KV cache quantization. Long-context amplifies the failure: at 8K tokens, uniform 4-bit degrades 11.15× baseline while constrained MCKP degrades only 1.23× — a 9× gap in degradation rate.\n\n2. **A cardinality constraint is the universal fix — and makes solver choice irrelevant**: A simple cardinality constraint (max_2bit ≤ k) is sufficient to prevent compounding across ALL tested architectures. Three universally beneficial properties: (a) prevents catastrophic over-allocation on sensitive architectures (Qwen: 32.45 → 10.91), (b) prevents moderate over-allocation on flat architectures (Gemma-2: 8.85 → 6.17, reducing 2-bit heads from 106 to 8), (c) reduces the feasible set to where solver choice is irrelevant — constrained greedy and constrained MCKP produce IDENTICAL bit allocations and PPL (Δ=0.0000). The constraint is parameterizable via small-scale compounding test (k≤8 universally safe: <2.5% degradation across all architectures). Practical implication: practitioners need only add one integer parameter to existing pipelines.\n\n3. **Non-uniform allocation benefit is rare — most models should use uniform 4-bit**: Under moderate compression (4×), only 1/8 tested architectures (Qwen2.5-7B, \"spread\" sensitivity pattern) benefits from non-uniform allocation (+27.3% PPL, +1.9pp downstream avg). The remaining 7/8 show no benefit or minor degradation (<1pp avg downstream). A 2-metric empirical diagnostic (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70) correctly classifies all 9 tested models (9/9 accuracy), providing practitioners a simple check: if the diagnostic says \"no\" — skip profiling and use uniform 4-bit with zero quality loss. This is the first systematic study of *when* non-uniform KV cache quantization is beneficial, correcting the implicit assumption that it always helps.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Per-head mixed-precision KV cache quantization promises better quality-compression tradeoffs than uniform bit-width. But on hardware-aligned non-consecutive bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, we discover that existing allocation algorithms (greedy, MCKP) systematically FAIL — producing worse results than naive uniform 4-bit across ALL tested architectures. The failure mode is unreported: 2-bit quantization distortions compound non-additively, and solvers consistently over-allocate 2-bit heads. Meanwhile, the field implicitly assumes non-uniform allocation always helps, but no systematic study has tested this across architectures.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: RateQuant provides R-D optimal per-head allocation via continuous closed-form and discrete greedy (optimal on consecutive integers {2,...,6}). KIVI and ARKV apply uniform or heuristic mixed-precision. However, on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}: (a) RateQuant's greedy produces PPL 32.45 vs optimal ~10.91 — polymatroid optimality breaks, (b) unconstrained MCKP fares even worse (PPL 36.92) due to compounding, (c) NO prior work addresses *when* non-uniform allocation is actually beneficial vs when uniform suffices.\n\n- **Our framing**: We present three contributions: (1) the first characterization of 2-bit compounding effects in per-head KV cache quantization — showing that profiling non-additivity causes ALL unconstrained solvers to fail on {2,4,8,16} across 8/8 architectures; (2) a simple universal fix: a cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) that prevents compounding, makes solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000), and is safely parameterizable (k≤8 universally safe); (3) the first systematic study of *when* non-uniform allocation helps — answer: rarely (1/8 architectures at moderate compression), with a 2-metric diagnostic (9/9 correct) that tells practitioners whether to invest in profiling or just use uniform 4-bit.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"We show that per-head KV cache quantization on hardware-aligned bit-widths has a universal failure mode: 2-bit distortions compound non-additively, causing ALL unconstrained solvers to underperform uniform 4-bit across 8 architectures. A cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) universally fixes this, making solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000). Surprisingly, under moderate compression, only 1/8 architectures benefits from non-uniform allocation at all — most models should simply use uniform 4-bit. A 2-metric diagnostic (9/9 accuracy) provides practitioners a simple check to determine when profiling is worthwhile. At long context (8K tokens), the constraint reduces degradation from 11.15× to 1.23× baseline, demonstrating critical deployment value.\"\n\n## \"When Does Non-Uniform Allocation Help?\" — Analysis Chapter\n\nFive case studies representing the full spectrum of heterogeneity:\n\n| Case | Model | GQA | Top-5% Conc. | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Role in Paper |\n|------|-------|-----|--------------|------------------------------|---------------|\n| **Strong positive** | Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 0.59-0.66 | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Primary showcase; \"spread\" pattern (L0 cluster, 4 heads, 26× dominance) |\n| **GQA counterexample** | Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 0.71 (hires) | ≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22) | Highest GQA but no benefit; \"spike\" pattern (L4H3 single outlier, 64% of total delta) |\n| **Marginal** | Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 0.57 (hires) | +0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47) | Boundary condition; constraint never binds (natural k=2) |\n| **Negative** | Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 0.22 (hires) | -0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13) | Profiler zero-signal; monotonic k-PPL curve |\n| **Strongest negative** | Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 0.23 (hires) | -0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03) | Low-end anchor; most uniform sensitivity (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) |\n\n**Spike vs Spread insight**: Yi-1.5 vs Qwen illustrates why GQA ratio alone is insufficient. Both have high GQA (8:1 vs 7:1), but Qwen's L0 *cluster* of sensitive heads creates optimization opportunities for MCKP, while Yi-1.5's single extreme outlier (L4H3) cannot be exploited — the solver assigns 8-bit to that one head but has no other heads to differentiate. Distribution shape matters more than the existence of outliers.\n\n**Compression amplifies benefit**: Even on low-heterogeneity Llama, aggressive 5.3× compression yields constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 (45× better).\n\n**Joint diagnostic** (n=8, 8/8 correct): concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 → non-uniform allocation recommended (spread pattern). Either condition violated → uniform suffices at moderate compression; non-uniform still valuable at aggressive compression. Yi-1.5 (concentration 0.71 but t₁/t₅=0.90 — spike), CodeLlama (0.80, t₁/t₅=0.81 — spike), and Qwen (0.61, t₁/t₅=0.57 — spread) illustrate why concentration alone is insufficient.\n\n## Solver Equivalence Evidence (plan_016, CONFIRMED ✅)\n\n| Method | PPL | Bit Distribution | Budget |\n|--------|-----|-------------------|--------|\n| Greedy unconstrained | 32.45 | {2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10} | 0.25 |\n| MCKP unconstrained | 36.92 | — | 0.25 |\n| **Greedy + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n| **MCKP + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n| Uniform 4-bit | 15.4454 | all 4-bit | 0.25 |\n\nKey takeaway: The constraint is the primary intervention — without it, both solvers fail; with it, solver choice is irrelevant (Δ=0.0000). This powerfully demonstrates the constraint is THE contribution.\n\n## Cross-Architecture Evidence Summary\n\n| Model | GQA | KV Heads | Top-5% Conc. | Unconstrained ×baseline (W2 v2) | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Distribution Shape | Conclusion |\n|-------|-----|----------|--------------|--------------------------------|------------------------------|-------------------|------------|\n| Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 112 | **0.61** | **3.31× (32.45)** ☠️ | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Spread (L0 cluster, 4 heads) | ✅ Strong benefit |\n| Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 192 | **0.71** (hires) | 1.08× (7.56) | **≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22)** | Spike (L4H3 single outlier) | ❌ GQA counterexample |\n| Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 256 | **0.57** (hires) | 1.07× (8.63) | **+0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47)** | Spike (t₁/t₅≈0.85, single dominant L2H5) | ≈ Marginal |\n| Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 256 | **0.22** (hires) | 1.08× (7.57) | **-0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13)** | Flat (profiler zero-signal) | ❌ Negative |\n| Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 336 | **0.23** (hires) | 1.47× (8.85) | **-0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03)** | Flat (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) | ❌ Strongest negative |\n\n**Unconstrained pattern** (W2 v2, all WikiText-2 test eval, gradient narrative): Unconstrained degradation follows a **concentration-dependent gradient**, not a binary catastrophe/benign split:\n- **Spread** (Qwen, conc=0.61): **3.31×** catastrophic — L0 cluster creates massive compounding\n- **Flat-high-2bit** (Gemma-2, conc=0.23): **1.47×** moderate — solver assigns 106/336=31.5% heads to 2-bit because distortions are indistinguishable (CV=1.28), cumulative effect significant despite small per-head delta\n- **Spike/Flat-low-2bit** (Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×): mild — solver selects few 2-bit heads (Yi 11.5%, Llama 4.7%, Mistral 16.4%)\n- In ALL cases unconstrained ≤ uniform 4-bit — solver consistently over-allocates 2-bit heads\n\n**Gemma-2 1.47× must be discussed in paper** (Reviewer mandate, severity: warning):\n\nThree-tier labeling (NOT binary catastrophe/benign):\n- **Catastrophic** (3.31×): Spread model (Qwen) — L0 cluster compounding\n- **Moderate** (1.47×): Flat-high-2bit (Gemma-2) — solver over-allocation from indistinguishable distortions\n- **Mild** (1.07-1.08×): Spike/Flat-low-2bit (Yi, Llama, Mistral)\n\nReviewer-suggested paragraph for paper (1 段, 3-4 句):\n\"Gemma-2-9B exhibits a moderate 1.47× degradation under unconstrained allocation, higher than the 1.07–1.08× observed in other non-Spread models. This stems from its flat sensitivity distribution (concentration 0.23, CV 1.28): the solver cannot meaningfully differentiate heads, leading to 31.5% of heads assigned to 2-bit (vs 4.7–16.4% in other models). While not catastrophic, this over-allocation still motivates the cardinality constraint even on flat-distribution architectures. The constraint reduces 2-bit heads from 106 to 8, yielding PPL within 0.3% of uniform — confirming that the constraint universally prevents solver over-allocation regardless of distribution shape.\"\n\nThis **strengthens** the paper: (1) honesty → credibility, (2) constraint has universal value (not just Spread), (3) explains solver degradation mechanism under low signal → added insight depth.\n\n⚠️ **Data file note**: `artifacts/w2_unconstrained_v2_results.json` still has old Gemma-2 BOS bug data (baseline=711.6). Fix in `artifacts/w2_gemma2_bos_fix_results.json`. Agent tasked to merge.\n\n**Key pattern**: Constrained allocation benefit depends on the joint condition (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70, 5/5 correct), NOT GQA ratio or concentration alone. Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, concentration 0.71 — highest — yet no benefit) vs Qwen (GQA 7:1, concentration 0.61, +27.3%) demonstrates that neither GQA nor concentration alone is a reliable proxy. The critical factor is sensitivity *distribution shape*: spread (multiple heads with cross-bitwidth gradients) enables MCKP, while spike (single outlier) or flat (uniform sensitivity) does not.\n\n**Aggressive compression** (Llama): At 5.3× compression, constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 — prevents catastrophic collapse even on low-heterogeneity architectures.\n\n### Mistral k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n\nPPL monotonically increases with k — every additional 2-bit head hurts. Even best k=4 (PPL 7.1648) is worse than uniform (7.131).\n\n| k | PPL | 2-bit | 4-bit | 8-bit | 16-bit | mem |\n|---|-----|-------|-------|-------|--------|-----|\n| 4 | **7.1648** | 4 | 252 | 0 | 0 | 0.248 |\n| 8 | 7.1997 | 8 | 247 | 0 | 1 | 0.249 |\n| 12 | 7.2448 | 12 | 242 | 0 | 2 | 0.250 |\n| 16 | 7.3106 | 16 | 238 | 0 | 2 | 0.248 |\n| 18 | 7.3231 | 18 | 235 | 0 | 3 | 0.250 |\n| uniform 4-bit | 7.131 | 0 | 256 | 0 | 0 | 0.250 |\n\nContrast with Qwen (U-shaped, optimal k=8) and Llama (flat, natural k=2). Mistral's monotonic pattern confirms profiler zero-signal: no head benefits from 2-bit downgrade.\n\n### Llama k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n\nAll k values produce identical PPL=8.4498. MCKP naturally selects only 2 heads for 2-bit — constraint never binds. Marginal +0.2% over uniform (8.4498 vs 8.469).\n\n### Downstream Eval — Cross-Architecture (W3, 0-shot, 5 tasks)\n\n**Qwen2.5-7B (Spread) — MCKP benefits translate to downstream** ✅\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP hires | Δ | BF16 Baseline |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|---------------|\n| ARC-C | 0.4812 | 0.5137 | **+3.16pp** | 0.5290 |\n| HellaSwag | 0.7284 | 0.7684 | **+4.00pp** | 0.7833 |\n| PIQA | 0.7661 | 0.7786 | **+1.25pp** | 0.7932 |\n| WinoGrande | 0.6622 | 0.6819 | **+1.97pp** | 0.6898 |\n| **Avg recovery** | — | — | **72.8%** | — |\n\n**Yi-1.5-9B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | 0.7946 | 0.7854 | -0.92pp |\n| arc_challenge | 0.5205 | 0.4881 | **-3.24pp** |\n| hellaswag | 0.5857 | 0.5797 | -0.60pp |\n| piqa | 0.7927 | 0.7894 | -0.33pp |\n| winogrande | 0.7174 | 0.7301 | +1.27pp |\n| **Average** | **0.6822** | **0.6745** | **-0.77pp** |\n\n**Llama-3.1-8B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | 0.8173 | 0.8039 | -1.34pp |\n| arc_challenge | 0.5256 | 0.4991 | **-2.65pp** |\n| hellaswag | 0.6026 | 0.6012 | -0.14pp |\n| piqa | 0.7867 | 0.7802 | -0.65pp |\n| winogrande | 0.7253 | 0.7238 | -0.15pp |\n| **Average** | **0.6915** | **0.6816** | **-0.99pp** |\n\n**Mistral-7B-v0.3 (Flat) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=4) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | — | — | — |\n| arc_challenge | — | — | — |\n| hellaswag | — | — | — |\n| piqa | — | — | — |\n| winogrande | — | — | — |\n| **Average** | **0.6894** | **0.6846** | **-0.48pp** |\n\n**Gemma-2-9B (Flat) — Negligible MCKP effect, noise range** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------|---|\n| **Average** | **0.7251** | **0.7265** | **+0.14pp** (noise) |\n\n**Downstream summary (Reviewer-verified framing)**:\n- Diagnostic correctly predicts both PPL and downstream outcomes across **all 5 tested models**\n- Spread (Qwen): consistent downstream gains (+1.25 to +4.00pp)\n- Non-Spread (4 models): MCKP shows **minor systematic degradation** vs uniform (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp noise)\n- **Llama signal**: 0/5 tasks where MCKP ≥ uniform — degradation is systematic, not task-specific noise\n- arc_challenge shows largest per-task effect (Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp)\n- **Paper must**: (a) report full per-task tables, not just averages, (b) use \"shows minor degradation\" NOT \"preserves accuracy\" — the latter has spin, (c) note arc_challenge as worst-case explicitly\n- **Limitation**: no multi-seed CI for downstream — 0-shot arc_challenge -3.24pp could be questioned for significance\n- **arc_challenge 系统性信号** (Reviewer 观察): arc_challenge 退化跨模型一致（Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp, Mistral -1.19pp, Gemma-2 -0.17pp），不是随机噪声。论文应主动讨论：\"ARC-Challenge shows the largest per-task sensitivity to allocation strategy, consistent with its reliance on multi-step reasoning where subtle KV cache errors accumulate.\"\n- **呈现方式**: 主表放完整 per-task 数据，文字用均值+range 概括。建议措辞：\"Across four non-Spread architectures, constrained MCKP shows minor average degradation vs uniform 4-bit (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp). Per-task variation ranges from +1.27pp (Yi, WinoGrande) to -3.24pp (Yi, ARC-Challenge).\"\n\n## Allocation Baseline Evidence (plan_015, mckp_reeval)\n\nAll numbers from unified bf16 eval pipeline, budget=0.25.\n\n| Model | Baseline | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | L0-random (mean±std) | L0-random (median) | Naive Positional | MCKP improvement |\n|-------|----------|---------------|------|----------------------|---------------------|------------------|------------------|\n| Qwen2.5-7B (k=8) | 9.8106 | 15.4454 | 10.9131 | 11.691±0.422 | **11.515** | 12.230 | 27.3% vs uniform (standard); 29.4% (hires, §5.4) |\n| Llama-3.1-8B (k=2) | 8.0918 | 8.469 | 8.4498 | 10.479±1.033 | **10.038** | 9.941 | +0.2% vs uniform |\n| Mistral-7B-v0.3 (k=4) | 7.035 | 7.131 | 7.1648 | 7.560±0.087 | **7.586** | 7.481 | -0.4% vs uniform |\n\n**Outlier note**: seed_4 inflates mean on Qwen (12.51) and Llama (12.44). Median is more robust: Qwen median 11.515 vs mean 11.691 (−0.176); Llama median 10.038 vs mean 10.479 (−0.441). Mistral has no outlier (median ≈ mean). Paper should report both mean±std and median.\n\n**MCKP vs L0-random (median)**: Qwen 10.91 vs 11.52 (−5.2%); Llama 8.45 vs 10.04 (−15.8%); Mistral 7.16 vs 7.59 (−5.7%). MCKP consistently outperforms random L0-constrained allocation across all architectures.\n\n## Differentiation from RateQuant\n\n| Aspect | RateQuant | Ours |\n|--------|-----------|------|\n| Bit-width selection | Greedy on consecutive integers {2,...,6} (Prop. 6 optimal) + continuous closed-form (Thm. 2) | Cardinality-constrained allocation on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}-bit |\n| Distortion model | Additive, parametric D(b)=α·β^{-b} | Additive + cardinality regularization for non-additivity |\n| Compounding effects | Acknowledged (Appendix M) but unaddressed | **Core contribution**: cardinality constraint prevents compounding; first quantitative evidence |\n| Action space | Consecutive integers (polymatroid → greedy optimal) | Non-consecutive hardware-aligned (polymatroid breaks → constraint needed, solver doesn't matter) |\n| Solver requirement | Greedy (provably optimal in their setting) | **Any solver** — constrained greedy = constrained MCKP (Δ=0.0000 PPL) |\n| K/V allocation | Asymmetric K/V budget (e.g. K=2.85, V=2.15) | MCKP/greedy treats K/V heads as independent items (natural extension) |\n| **Applicability analysis** | **Not addressed — assumes non-uniform always helps** | **Systematic study of when non-uniform allocation is beneficial (new contribution)** |\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **\"The constraint is just a heuristic, not a real contribution\"**: Strongest reviewer attack under new framing. Defense: (a) principled motivation from compounding effect non-additivity with first quantitative evidence, (b) constraint parameterization via systematic compounding test, (c) the finding that constraint alone makes solver choice irrelevant is a surprising and practically useful result — practitioners need only add one parameter to existing pipelines.\n- **Incrementality over RateQuant**: Defense: (a) RateQuant's greedy is suboptimal unconstrained on {2,4,8,16} (PPL 32.45), (b) our constraint fixes RateQuant's greedy to match MCKP — we're improving their method, not replacing it, (c) applicability analysis is entirely new.\n- **Method only strong on one architecture (Qwen)**: 5 models tested, only Qwen shows clear benefit. Mitigate: (a) analysis contribution framing — characterizing boundary conditions is more useful than universal positive, (b) honest negative/marginal results (Yi-1.5, Gemma-2, Mistral, Llama) strengthen credibility, (c) unlike prior work that assumes non-uniform always helps, we provide the first systematic study of *when it fails*, (d) Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, FAIL) is particularly powerful — it disproves the naive \"higher GQA = more benefit\" hypothesis and shows our diagnostic is needed.\n- **GQA ratio is not a reliable proxy**: Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1) directly contradicts a GQA-based prediction. Do NOT present GQA ratio as a predictor — present it as one contributing factor. The reliable predictor is Top-5% concentration (0.50 threshold, 8/8 correct). The \"spike vs spread\" analysis explains WHY same-GQA models differ.\n- **Statistical power**: n=8 models is directional evidence, not statistical claim. Do NOT claim \"significant correlation\" — use \"consistent pattern across 8 architectures\" or \"8/8 correctly classified by the 0.50 threshold.\"\n- **No eviction arm**: Mention as negative finding; framework extends naturally to eviction.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"The cardinality constraint is trivial — just cap the extreme allocations\"** → (a) Trivial in retrospect, but without it both greedy (PPL 32.45) and MCKP (PPL 36.92) fail catastrophically — the failure mode is non-obvious, (b) principled motivation from compounding effect characterization (plan_004), (c) optimal k selection via systematic small-scale test, (d) the finding that this single intervention eliminates solver complexity is surprising and practically valuable.\n2. **\"This is just RateQuant with a constraint added\"** → (a) We agree — and that's the point: RateQuant's greedy + our constraint achieves identical results to MCKP + constraint, (b) the constraint addresses a real gap: compounding effects on {2,4,8,16} that RateQuant acknowledges but doesn't solve, (c) applicability analysis is new.\n3. **\"The method only works on Qwen — isn't this a Qwen paper?\"** → We systematically test 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1 and honestly report negative results (Gemma-2, Mistral). The analysis contribution — characterizing *boundary conditions* of non-uniform quantization — generalizes beyond any single model and is more useful than a universally positive but misleading claim.\n4. **\"How does this work at different compression ratios?\"** → Budget sweep across 2×, 4×, 8× (plan_005). Aggressive compression on Llama shows benefit amplifies even on low-heterogeneity models.\n5. **\"n=3/4/5 models is not enough for the heterogeneity claim\"** → Acknowledged as limitation. We present directional evidence across 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1, with a monotonic trend between GQA ratio, heterogeneity, and MCKP benefit. The Top-5% concentration diagnostic is a testable hypothesis, not a statistical claim.\n6. **\"RateQuant does K/V asymmetric allocation, do you?\"** → Framework naturally treats K and V heads as independent items; plan_014 tests K/V separation.\n7. **\"Where are the downstream task results?\"** → ✅ DONE (plan_012 + W3, all 5 models): Qwen (Spread): +1.25 to +4.00pp across 4 tasks, 72.8% avg recovery. Yi-1.5 (Spike): avg -0.77pp. Llama (Spike): avg -0.99pp (0/5 tasks positive — systematic). Mistral (Flat): avg -0.48pp. Gemma-2 (Flat): avg +0.14pp (noise). **Diagnostic predicts both PPL and downstream correctly across all 5 architectures**. Must report full per-task tables; use \"shows minor degradation\" not \"preserves accuracy\".\n8. **\"The profiler distortion=0.0 on Mistral suggests the profiling method is broken\"** → Profiler correctly reports near-zero sensitivity differences. Some architectures genuinely have homogeneous head sensitivity, making non-uniform allocation futile.\n9. **\"If solver doesn't matter, why present MCKP at all?\"** → (a) MCKP provides the formal framework for the constrained allocation problem — it's the lens through which we analyze the problem even if greedy solves it equally well, (b) presenting both solvers with identical results IS the evidence that the constraint is what matters, (c) for future extensions (more bit-widths, per-layer budgets), MCKP may regain advantage — we keep it as general framework.\n","numLines":234,"startLine":1,"totalLines":234}}}
